        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AttestedCredentialData">
            <summary>
            Represents attested credential data included in authenticator data during credential creation.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Attested credential data contains:
            - 16 bytes: AAGUID (Authenticator Attestation GUID)
            - 2 bytes: Credential ID length (big-endian)
            - L bytes: Credential ID
            - Variable: COSE public key (CBOR-encoded)
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-2/#sctn-attested-credential-data
            </para>
            <para>
            Parse copies the credential ID and encoded key. It extracts one CBOR value for the key without
            requiring a COSE map, alg or algorithm-specific parameters. Decode the key separately and apply
            RP algorithm/trust policy; extraction is not attestation or mathematical-key verification.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AttestedCredentialData.MinimumLength">
            <summary>
            Minimum size of attested credential data (AAGUID + length field).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AttestedCredentialData.Aaguid">
            <summary>
            Gets the Authenticator Attestation GUID identifying the authenticator model.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AttestedCredentialData.CredentialId">
            <summary>
            Gets the credential ID.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AttestedCredentialData.CredentialPublicKey">
            <summary>
            Gets the COSE-encoded public key.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AttestedCredentialData.Parse(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.Int32@)">
            <summary>
            Parses attested credential data from raw bytes.
            </summary>
            <param name="data">The raw data starting at attested credential data.</param>
            <param name="bytesRead">The number of bytes consumed from the input.</param>
            <returns>The parsed AttestedCredentialData.</returns>
            <remarks>Consumes this structure, not any following authenticator extension suffix.</remarks>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The fixed prefix or declared credential ID is too short.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.Formats.Cbor.CborContentException">The following encoded CBOR value cannot be read.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData">
            <summary>
            Represents the authenticator data structure as defined in WebAuthn/CTAP specifications.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The authenticator data is a binary structure that contains:
            - 32 bytes: RP ID hash (SHA-256)
            - 1 byte: Flags
            - 4 bytes: Signature counter (big-endian uint32)
            - (optional) Attested credential data
            - (optional) Extensions data (CBOR)
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-2/#sctn-authenticator-data
            for the base layout. BE/BS meanings are defined in WebAuthn Level 3, Recommendation 25 August
            2026, §6.1.3 (https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/REC-webauthn-3-20260825/#sctn-credential-backup).
            </para>
            <para>
            Parse copies the full input, RP hash, attested fields and extension suffix into independent storage.
            RawData preserves authenticator data, not a surrounding CTAP response. Extension/raw bytes can contain
            secret-derived material; this type has no disposal/zeroing API. Do not log that material or assume
            clearing the original input or disposing a session clears these copies.
            </para>
            <para>
            Flags report received bits, not independently verified events. Parsing and RP-hash comparison do not
            verify a signature, origin/challenge, account binding, requested policy or attestation trust.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.MinimumLength">
            <summary>
            Minimum size of authenticator data (rpIdHash + flags + signCount).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.RpIdHash">
            <summary>
            Gets the SHA-256 hash of the Relying Party ID.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.Flags">
            <summary>
            Gets the authenticator data flags.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.SignCount">
            <summary>
            Gets the signature counter value.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            The authenticator can use a per-credential or global counter, or report zero without counter
            support. The RP compares stored state and chooses a risk policy (WebAuthn L2 §6.1.1); this SDK
            enforces no monotonicity. A counter mismatch is not certain proof of cloning.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.AttestedCredentialData">
            <summary>
            Gets the attested credential data, if present (when AT flag is set).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.Extensions">
            <summary>
            Gets the CBOR-encoded extensions data, if present (when ED flag is set).
            </summary>
            <remarks>Copies the complete remaining suffix without checking that it is one complete CBOR map.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.RawData">
            <summary>
            Gets the raw authenticator data bytes.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.UserPresent">
            <summary>
            Gets whether the received UP bit reports user presence.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.UserVerified">
            <summary>
            Gets whether the received UV bit reports user verification.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.BackupEligible">
            <summary>
            Gets whether the received BE bit reports that this credential is backup eligible.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.BackedUp">
            <summary>
            Gets whether the received BS bit reports that this credential is currently backed up.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.HasAttestedCredentialData">
            <summary>
            Gets a value indicating whether attested credential data is present.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.HasExtensions">
            <summary>
            Gets a value indicating whether extension data is present.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.Parse(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Parses authenticator data from raw bytes.
            </summary>
            <param name="data">The raw authenticator data bytes.</param>
            <returns>The parsed AuthenticatorData.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Checks the 37-byte prefix and parses attested data when AT is set. With ED set, the remaining
            bytes are copied without extension-map validation; with ED unset, trailing bytes are retained
            in RawData but otherwise ignored. It does not enforce all flag relationships or ceremony rules.
            </remarks>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The fixed prefix or declared attested fields are too short.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.Formats.Cbor.CborContentException">An extracted attested CBOR value cannot be read.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.Parse(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Parses authenticator data from memory.
            </summary>
            <param name="data">The raw authenticator data.</param>
            <returns>The parsed AuthenticatorData.</returns>
            <remarks>Copies storage and applies the same parsing limits as the span overload.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorData.VerifyRpIdHash(System.String)">
            <summary>
            Compares the received RP ID hash with SHA-256 of the UTF-8-encoded expected RP ID.
            </summary>
            <param name="rpId">The expected RP ID string.</param>
            <returns>True if the hash matches, false otherwise.</returns>
            <remarks>A match is only this hash comparison, not origin authorization or complete RP assertion verification.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags">
            <summary>
            Flags for authenticator data as defined in WebAuthn specification.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags.None">
            <summary>
            No flags set.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags.UserPresent">
            <summary>
            User present result (UP).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags.RFU1">
            <summary>
            Reserved for future use (RFU1).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags.UserVerified">
            <summary>
            User verified result (UV).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags.BackupEligibility">
            <summary>
            Backup eligibility (BE).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags.BackupState">
            <summary>
            Backup state (BS).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags.RFU2">
            <summary>
            Reserved for future use (RFU2).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags.AttestedCredentialData">
            <summary>
            Attested credential data included (AT).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.AuthenticatorDataFlags.ExtensionData">
            <summary>
            Extension data included (ED).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.Ctap2CredentialOptions">
            <summary>
            Credential reader options pre-configured for CTAP2 operations.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.Ctap2CredentialOptions.ForCtap2Pin">
            <summary>
            Creates a FIDO2 PIN prompt preset with console-reader limits of 4–63 UTF-16 characters.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            ConsoleCredentialReader counts char values before converting with the default UTF-8 encoding,
            not UTF-8 bytes or Unicode code points. Non-ASCII text can exceed 63 encoded bytes. This preset
            does not enforce the authenticator's current minimum or full CTAP PIN rules; the input layer must
            validate NFC UTF-8, code-point/byte limits and no final NUL before submitting PIN bytes.
            Dispose the credential reader's returned memory owner after the awaited operation to clear its secret.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions">
            <summary>
            Options for the GetAssertion operation.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            These options correspond to CTAP2 authenticatorGetAssertion parameters:
            - allowList (0x03): List of allowed credentials
            - extensions (0x04): Extension inputs
            - options (0x05): Boolean options (up, uv)
            - pinUvAuthParam (0x06): PIN/UV auth parameter
            - pinUvAuthProtocol (0x07): PIN/UV protocol version
            </para>
            <para>
            The mutable object retains supplied lists and byte memory. Keep it and borrowed input storage
            unchanged through the awaited command; read-only views are not immutable snapshots. The caller
            clears auth parameters and secret-bearing inputs after completion, including failure. This type
            does not negotiate capabilities, choose RP account policy or verify returned assertions.
            Setting auth properties establishes no persistent logged-in state; the authenticator governs token
            scope, permission consumption and expiry for the request.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.AllowList">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the list of allowed credentials.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            A nonempty list restricts the authenticator's credential search to these descriptors for the RP.
            Null/empty lists are omitted and request discovery by RP ID, subject to authorization and
            credential-protection policy. The list and descriptor ID storage are borrowed.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.UserPresence">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets whether user presence is required.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Null omits up (CTAP defaults to true); false explicitly requests no user-presence check, for
            example a preflight. Authenticator/extension policy can still reject it. This is not a promise
            of successful silent authentication; WebAuthn RP assertions ordinarily require UP.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.UserVerification">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the CTAP uv option requesting built-in user verification.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Null omits uv; false still sends the key. CTAP 2.1/2.3 §6.2 prohibit uv alongside PinUvAuthParam,
            even false; omit it for token authorization and when built-in UV is unsupported. This setter
            neither obtains a PIN nor enforces the combination. Check received UV and perform RP verification.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.PinUvAuthParam">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the PIN/UV auth parameter for authorization.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Authenticate the exact clientDataHash with a valid token and matching protocol. Permission-bearing
            tokens need GetAssertion permission and RP scope; actual state/lifetime is enforced by the
            authenticator. Omit UserVerification. Null/empty auth bytes are omitted, not encoded as a
            zero-length probe; tag size/permissions are not checked here. The memory remains caller-owned.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.PinUvAuthProtocol">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the PIN/UV auth protocol version.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Match the auth parameter's protocol. Null defaults to encoded version 2 only with nonempty auth
            bytes; this is not protocol negotiation. A protocol without auth bytes is omitted.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.Extensions">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets extension inputs as a CBOR-encoded map.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Borrowed bytes are emitted without extension capability/policy validation. Null/zero-byte input
            is omitted, whereas an encoded empty CBOR map is present.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.#ctor">
            <summary>
            Creates default options.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.WithUserVerification(System.Boolean)">
            <summary>
            Sets the user verification option.
            </summary>
            <param name="value">The built-in UV request value; this setter does not clear token authentication.</param>
            <returns>This options instance for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.WithPinUvAuth(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Int32)">
            <summary>
            Sets the PIN/UV authentication parameters.
            </summary>
            <param name="param">Caller-owned auth parameter over clientDataHash; keep stable through the awaited command.</param>
            <param name="protocol">The protocol version.</param>
            <returns>This options instance for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.WithAllowList(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList{Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor})">
            <summary>
            Sets the allow list.
            </summary>
            <param name="allowList">The allowed credentials.</param>
            <returns>This options instance for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.WithAllowList(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte}[])">
            <summary>
            Sets the allow list from credential IDs.
            </summary>
            <param name="credentialIds">The allowed IDs; the new descriptor list still borrows each ID's byte storage.</param>
            <returns>This options instance for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse">
            <summary>
            Represents the response from authenticatorGetAssertion.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            CTAP2 getAssertion response structure:
            - 0x01: credential (map) - selected credential; see <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.Credential"/> for version conditions
            - 0x02: authData (byte string) - authenticator data
            - 0x03: signature (byte string) - assertion signature
            - 0x04: user (map, optional) - authenticator-supplied account information
            - 0x05: numberOfCredentials (uint, optional) - total credentials for first response
            - 0x06: userSelected (bool, optional) - user selected this credential
            - 0x07: largeBlobKey (byte string, optional) - large blob key
            </para>
            <para>
            CTAP 2.3 §6.2.2 also defines unsigned extension outputs at key 0x08. This decoder skips that
            field and other unknown outer fields; it does not retain a complete response envelope.
            </para>
            <para>
            Decoding copies byte strings, including the signature, IDs, large-blob key and authenticator data.
            Authenticator-data parsing creates further independent copies; <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.ExtensionOutputs"/>
            refers to its extension copy. Neither this result nor session disposal clears these buffers.
            Large-blob keys and secret-derived extension data are sensitive: do not log them or assume that
            clearing the original input clears the decoded copies. This type provides no disposal/zeroing API.
            </para>
            <para>
            Parsing is not authentication. The RP must verify the signature and client-data challenge/origin,
            credential/account binding, RP ID, required UP/UV and counter policy before accepting the assertion.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.Credential">
            <summary>
            Gets the credential descriptor for the selected credential.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            CTAP 2.0 §5.2 permits omission only when the request allowList contains exactly one descriptor,
            not merely when one credential matches. CTAP 2.1/2.3 §6.2.2 require this field. This decoder has
            no request/version context and exposes absence as null; it does not recover the requested ID.
            A caller handling the 2.0 exception must retain the known singleton descriptor for association.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.AuthenticatorData">
            <summary>
            Gets the authenticator data.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.AuthenticatorDataRaw">
            <summary>
            Gets the raw authenticator data bytes.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.Signature">
            <summary>
            Gets the received assertion signature bytes; their encoding depends on the credential algorithm.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.User">
            <summary>
            Gets the authenticator-supplied user entity, if present.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            CTAP 2.1/2.3 §6.2.2 require at least the opaque user ID for discoverable credentials and permit
            a user entity for server-side credentials. The ID is not conditional on UV. Authenticators MUST
            NOT return identifying name/displayName/icon fields without UV; this decoder passes modeled
            name/displayName through rather than enforcing that privacy rule, and skips icon. Use the ID,
            not display fields, for RP account binding and authorization. Names can be absent even with UV.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.NumberOfCredentials">
            <summary>
            Gets the total number of credentials matching the request.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            CTAP defaults an absent count to one; authenticator account selection can omit it even when
            multiple accounts exist. When a valid first-response count N exceeds one, collect N−1 next
            assertions promptly, without unrelated authenticator operations between calls. The SDK does
            not reserve the sequence or validate this uint32-to-int conversion against Int32.MaxValue.
            Next-assertion responses omit the count.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.UserSelected">
            <summary>
            Gets whether the user explicitly selected this credential.
            </summary>
            <remarks>Reports the received field, not an SDK account-picker result. CTAP defaults absence to false.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.LargeBlobKey">
            <summary>
            Gets the secret symmetric large-blob storage key from response key 0x07, if supplied.
            </summary>
            <remarks>Presence does not establish the required key length; the decoder does not check it.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.ExtensionOutputs">
            <summary>
            Gets the signed authenticator-data extension bytes, if the ED bit is set.
            </summary>
            <remarks>These bytes are not the unsigned output map at response key 0x08, and are not verified here.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.Decode(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Parses a getAssertion response from CBOR-encoded data.
            </summary>
            <param name="data">The CBOR-encoded response (excluding status byte).</param>
            <returns>The parsed response.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Uses a lax CBOR reader and checks authData/signature presence, but not signature nonemptiness,
            version-dependent fields, all conditional rules or complete input consumption. CBOR errors can
            raise <see cref="T:System.Formats.Cbor.CborContentException"/>; missing required modeled fields raise
            <see cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException"/>. Authenticator-data and entity checks can also fail.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.Decode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Parses a getAssertion response from a CBOR reader.
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader.</param>
            <returns>The parsed response.</returns>
            <remarks>Consumes one response map using the supplied reader; the same model/verification limits apply.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.GetCredentialId">
            <summary>
            Gets the credential ID from the credential descriptor or returns empty.
            </summary>
            <remarks>Empty reports a missing descriptor, not a recovered request ID or a failed signature verification.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.GetUserHandle">
            <summary>
            Gets the user handle from the user entity or returns empty.
            </summary>
            <remarks>Empty reports absence of the entity, not proof that no account exists or authentication failed.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions">
            <summary>
            Options for the MakeCredential operation.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            These options correspond to CTAP2 authenticatorMakeCredential parameters:
            - excludeList (0x05): List of credentials to exclude
            - extensions (0x06): Extension inputs
            - options (0x07): Boolean options (rk, up, uv)
            - pinUvAuthParam (0x08): PIN/UV auth parameter
            - pinUvAuthProtocol (0x09): PIN/UV protocol version
            - enterpriseAttestation (0x0A): Enterprise attestation type
            </para>
            <para>
            This mutable options object retains supplied lists and byte memory, not immutable snapshots.
            Keep it and its borrowed storage unchanged through the awaited command. The caller owns and clears
            auth-parameter/secret-bearing input buffers after completion, including failure; request cleanup
            does not clear them. These options encode requests, not capability negotiation or RP verification.
            Token authorization depends on authenticator state/permissions, not a persistent logged-in state
            established by setting these properties.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.ExcludeList">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the list of credentials to exclude.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Requests exclusion of these credentials under the authenticator's RP and authorization checks.
            This is not a global duplicate-user guarantee. Null/empty lists are omitted from the request;
            the supplied collection and descriptor IDs are borrowed.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.ResidentKey">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets whether to create a discoverable credential (resident key).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            True requests a credential discoverable by RP ID without supplying its ID. Support, storage
            capacity, authorization and credential-protection policy still apply. Null omits rk and false
            explicitly requests non-discoverable creation; neither describes where all key material is stored.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.UserPresence">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the "up" option key.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Defaults to omitted. Set <see langword="true"/> only when the key must be present on the wire
            (CTAP 2.1+ authenticators accept it; CTAP 2.0 may not). <see langword="false"/> is rejected with
            <see cref="T:System.ArgumentException"/>: CTAP 2.1-2.3 §6.1 says the value "MUST be true if present" and
            false yields CTAP2_ERR_INVALID_OPTION regardless of authenticator version. For a silent probe use
            getAssertion with up=false (§5 "pre-flight"), as the WebAuthn client does.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.UserVerification">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the CTAP uv option requesting built-in user verification.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Null omits the uv key; false still sends it. CTAP 2.1/2.3 §6.1 require platforms to omit uv if
            built-in UV is unsupported and to omit it whenever PinUvAuthParam is supplied, even when false.
            PIN authorization uses a token/auth parameter, not this option. The SDK does not enforce these
            combinations or obtain a PIN here. Inspect the returned UV bit, then apply RP verification policy.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.PinUvAuthParam">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the PIN/UV auth parameter for authorization.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Authenticate the exact 32-byte clientDataHash with a valid PIN/UV token and the matching protocol.
            Permission-bearing tokens require MakeCredential permission and the RP scope; authenticator
            state/lifetime still govern authorization. Omit UserVerification when using this parameter.
            Null/empty memory is omitted, so this surface does not encode a zero-length auth probe. The SDK
            does not validate tag length or token permissions here. The supplied memory remains caller-owned.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.PinUvAuthProtocol">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the PIN/UV auth protocol version.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Match the protocol used for PinUvAuthParam. With nonempty auth bytes, null encodes version 2;
            this is an encoding default, not negotiation. Without auth bytes, this field is omitted.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.EnterpriseAttestation">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the enterprise attestation type.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Values: 1 = vendor-facilitated, 2 = platform-managed.
            Requires advertised support, enabled configuration and applicable RP authorization. These
            options do not validate those conditions or the integer range; the response field reports use.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.Extensions">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets extension inputs as a CBOR-encoded map.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Borrowed encoded bytes are written as supplied, without extension capability/policy validation.
            Null/zero-byte input is omitted; an encoded empty CBOR map is still present on the wire.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.#ctor">
            <summary>
            Creates default options.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.WithResidentKey(System.Boolean)">
            <summary>
            Sets the discoverable credential (resident key) option.
            </summary>
            <param name="value">Whether to create a discoverable credential.</param>
            <returns>This options instance for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.WithUserVerification(System.Boolean)">
            <summary>
            Sets the user verification option.
            </summary>
            <param name="value">The built-in UV request value; this setter does not clear existing token authentication.</param>
            <returns>This options instance for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.WithPinUvAuth(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Int32)">
            <summary>
            Sets the PIN/UV authentication parameters.
            </summary>
            <param name="param">Caller-owned auth parameter over clientDataHash; keep stable through the awaited command.</param>
            <param name="protocol">The protocol version.</param>
            <returns>This options instance for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.WithExcludeList(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList{Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor})">
            <summary>
            Sets the exclude list.
            </summary>
            <param name="excludeList">The credentials to exclude.</param>
            <returns>This options instance for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse">
            <summary>
            Represents the response from authenticatorMakeCredential.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Exposes the received authenticator data and attestation statement for registration processing.
            Decoding does not verify the attestation signature, certificate chain, challenge/origin, RP/account
            binding, required UP/UV or RP attestation policy. Those checks belong to the RP registration workflow.
            </para>
            <para>
            CTAP2 makeCredential response structure:
            - 0x01: fmt (text string) - attestation statement format
            - 0x02: authData (byte string) - authenticator data
            - 0x03: attStmt (map) - attestation statement
            - 0x04: epAtt (bool, optional) - enterprise attestation used
            - 0x05: largeBlobKey (byte string, optional) - large blob key
            - 0x06: unsignedExtensionOutputs (map, optional) - unsigned outputs (CTAP 2.3 §6.1)
            </para>
            <para>
            Decode borrows attestation-statement and unsigned-output slices from the input buffer. Keep that
            buffer unchanged while these views are used. Authenticator-data byte strings, parsed authenticator
            fields and largeBlobKey are independent copies. This result has no disposal/zeroing API, and session
            disposal does not clear it. Clearing the input cannot clear independent secret-bearing copies;
            do not log large-blob keys or secret-derived extension data.
            </para>
            <para>
            Unknown outer fields are skipped, not retained in a complete RawData envelope. Raw authenticator
            data and attestation-statement bytes preserve only their respective nested structures.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.Format">
            <summary>
            Gets the attestation statement format identifier.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Common formats: "packed", "tpm", "android-key", "android-safetynet", 
            "fido-u2f", "apple", "none"
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.AuthenticatorData">
            <summary>
            Gets the parsed authenticator data; the decoder does not require the AT bit or new credential data.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.AuthenticatorDataRaw">
            <summary>
            Gets the raw authenticator data bytes.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.AttestationStatement">
            <summary>
            Gets the parsed or opaque attestation statement, not a verified attestation result.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.EnterpriseAttestation">
            <summary>
            Gets whether enterprise attestation was used.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.LargeBlobKey">
            <summary>
            Gets the secret symmetric large-blob storage key from response key 0x05, if supplied.
            </summary>
            <remarks>The decoder does not validate key length or whether the extension was requested.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.ExtensionOutputs">
            <summary>
            Gets the signed authenticator-data extension bytes, if the ED bit is set.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.UnsignedExtensionOutputs">
            <summary>
            Gets the unsigned extension outputs from makeCredential response key 0x06.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            CTAP 2.3 §6.1 defines text extension identifiers mapped to unsigned values. Each value here is
            its complete encoded CBOR slice, not necessarily a CBOR byte string, and borrows the input buffer.
            An empty map and an omitted field must be treated equivalently by clients, although this model
            preserves empty versus null. These values are separate from signed authData outputs; extensions
            such as experimental previewSign can carry proof objects that require their own verification.
            WebAuthn client-extension processing is a separate layer, not this integer-key envelope.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.Decode(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Parses a makeCredential response from CBOR-encoded data.
            </summary>
            <param name="data">The CBOR-encoded response (excluding status byte).</param>
            <returns>The parsed response.</returns>
            <remarks>
            The input is borrowed as described on this type. Uses lax CBOR parsing and requires fmt,
            authData and attStmt, but does not enforce every attestation shape or complete envelope consumption.
            CBOR failures can raise <see cref="T:System.Formats.Cbor.CborContentException"/>; missing modeled required fields raise
            <see cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException"/>. Authenticator-data parsing can also reject short input.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.Decode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Parses a makeCredential response from a CBOR reader.
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader.</param>
            <returns>The parsed response.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Consumes one encoded value and applies the memory decoder's checks. Attestation and unsigned
            values can reference the reader's underlying buffer; keep it unchanged while those views are used.
            This overload is not a complete-input or cryptographic-verification boundary.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.DecodeInternal(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader,System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Decodes one response map while retaining slices of the borrowed response bytes.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.ParseAttestationFormat(System.String)">
            <summary>
            Parses the attestation format string into the AttestationFormat type.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.GetCredentialId">
            <summary>
            Gets the credential ID from the attested credential data.
            </summary>
            <returns>The credential ID, or empty if not present.</returns>
            <remarks>Empty is a helper fallback, not proof that a makeCredential response satisfies the protocol.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.GetCredentialPublicKey">
            <summary>
            Gets the credential public key from the attested credential data.
            </summary>
            <returns>The COSE-encoded public key, or empty if not present.</returns>
            <remarks>The attested-data parser extracts the encoding without verifying key structure or mathematical validity.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse.GetAaguid">
            <summary>
            Gets the AAGUID from the attested credential data.
            </summary>
            <returns>The AAGUID, or <see cref="F:System.Guid.Empty"/> if not present.</returns>
            <remarks>Guid.Empty can also be received on the wire; inspect AttestedCredentialData to distinguish absence.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor">
            <summary>
            Represents a public key credential descriptor used in exclude/allow lists.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Per WebAuthn/CTAP specification, a credential descriptor identifies a credential
            by its type and ID, with optional transport hints.
            </para>
            <para>
            Constructors borrow ID memory and the transport collection; keep them stable during use and
            through an awaited request. Parse materializes new ID/transport storage. Transport hints are
            metadata, not proof that an interface is reachable, and Encode writes only modeled fields.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-2/#dictdef-publickeycredentialdescriptor
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor.PublicKeyType">
            <summary>
            The credential type (always "public-key" for WebAuthn).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor.Type">
            <summary>
            Gets the credential type.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor.Id">
            <summary>
            Gets the credential ID.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor.Transports">
            <summary>
            Gets the optional transport hints.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.String,System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList{System.String})">
            <summary>
            Creates a new credential descriptor.
            </summary>
            <param name="id">The nonempty credential ID; its storage is borrowed without copying.</param>
            <param name="type">The credential type (default: "public-key").</param>
            <param name="transports">Optional borrowed transport hints; no immutable snapshot is made.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor.FromCredentialId(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Creates a credential descriptor from a credential ID.
            </summary>
            <param name="credentialId">The credential ID bytes.</param>
            <returns>A new credential descriptor.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor.Parse(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Parses a credential descriptor from CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader positioned at the descriptor.</param>
            <returns>The parsed credential descriptor.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialDescriptor.Encode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborWriter)">
            <summary>
            Encodes this descriptor as CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="writer">The CBOR writer.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialRpEntity">
            <summary>
            Represents a relying party entity.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Per WebAuthn/CTAP specification, the relying party entity describes the
            relying party responsible for the request.
            </para>
            <para>
            The constructor checks only nonempty ID text, not domain syntax or authorization against an origin.
            The client must establish a valid RP ID and client-data binding; the RP verifies the ceremony.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-2/#dictdef-publickeycredentialrpentity
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialRpEntity.Id">
            <summary>
            Gets the relying party identifier.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialRpEntity.Name">
            <summary>
            Gets the relying party name for display.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialRpEntity.#ctor(System.String,System.String)">
            <summary>
            Creates a new RP entity.
            </summary>
            <param name="id">The RP identifier (typically a domain name).</param>
            <param name="name">Optional display name.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialRpEntity.Parse(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Parses an RP entity from CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader.</param>
            <returns>The parsed RP entity.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialRpEntity.Encode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborWriter)">
            <summary>
            Encodes this RP entity as CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="writer">The CBOR writer.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity">
            <summary>
            Represents account information for credential creation or an authenticator response.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Id is an opaque RP-scoped account handle, not display text. WebAuthn L2 §5.4.3 requires RP
            authentication/authorization decisions to use the ID rather than name/displayName; the handle
            must not contain personally identifying information. Response identifying fields can be absent
            and are prohibited without authenticator UV under CTAP 2.1/2.3 §6.2.2.
            </para>
            <para>
            The public constructor requires a nonempty ID of at most 64 bytes and nonempty name/displayName.
            These are current SDK restrictions: CTAP permits omitted display inputs for privacy and permits
            an empty account ID (though it recommends avoiding it); WebAuthn's nonempty handle rule is narrower.
            Parse permits absent display fields but still rejects empty/oversized IDs. Constructors borrow ID
            memory; Parse creates an independent ID array. Keep borrowed bytes stable during use/transmission.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-2/#dictdef-publickeycredentialuserentity
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity.Id">
            <summary>
            Gets the opaque RP-scoped user handle used for account binding, not a human-readable name.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity.Name">
            <summary>
            Gets the human-readable user name.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            This may be null when parsing a GetAssertion response, as only the user ID is required.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity.DisplayName">
            <summary>
            Gets the human-readable display name.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            This may be null when parsing a GetAssertion response, as only the user ID is required.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.String,System.String)">
            <summary>
            Creates a new user entity.
            </summary>
            <param name="id">The nonempty user handle (up to 64 bytes); byte storage is borrowed.</param>
            <param name="name">The nonempty name required by this SDK constructor, not an authorization identifier.</param>
            <param name="displayName">The nonempty display name required by this SDK constructor.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.String,System.String,System.Boolean)">
            <summary>
            Internal constructor for parsing responses where name/displayName may be absent.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity.Parse(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Parses a user entity from CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader.</param>
            <returns>The parsed user entity.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Requires an ID and copies its bytes; name/displayName are optional and unknown fields are skipped.
            This parser does not filter identifying fields based on UV or complete RP account verification.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity.Encode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborWriter)">
            <summary>
            Encodes this user entity as CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="writer">The CBOR writer.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Crypto.EncryptedMetadataDecryptor">
            <summary>
            Decrypts optional GetInfo device-identifier and credential-store-state fields using
            keys derived from a persistent PIN/UV auth token (PPUAT).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            CTAP 2.3 §6.4 defines encIdentifier as a 128-bit device identifier and encCredStoreState as
            an opaque 128-bit credential-store state. Each output is a fresh 16-byte IV followed by
            16 bytes of AES-128-CBC ciphertext. They are not per-credential identifiers. Use the matching
            persistent token, not an arbitrary ordinary PIN/UV token. These offline helpers do not check
            device capabilities, token permissions or the standard field lengths; they accept generic
            block-aligned ciphertext, including IV-only input.
            </para>
            <para>
            CBC without padding is not authenticated encryption: a wrong token can return plausible bytes.
            A null result is not reliable wrong-token detection. Inputs are borrowed for the call; returned
            plaintext and derived keys are caller-owned. Clear those arrays with
            CryptographicOperations.ZeroMemory when finished, including after later processing fails.
            Clearing the helper's stack key does not guarantee cleanup of all provider or failure-output copies.
            </para>
            <para>
            HKDF parameters:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>Algorithm: SHA-256</description></item>
              <item><description>Secret: PPUAT (PIN/UV Auth Token)</description></item>
              <item><description>Salt: 32 zero bytes</description></item>
              <item><description>Info: "encIdentifier" or "encCredStoreState"</description></item>
              <item><description>Output length: 16 bytes (AES-128 key)</description></item>
            </list>
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Crypto.EncryptedMetadataDecryptor.DecryptIdentifier(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Decrypts the encIdentifier field using PPUAT-derived key.
            </summary>
            <param name="ppuat">The Persistent PIN/UV Auth Token.</param>
            <param name="encIdentifier">Borrowed IV-prefixed encIdentifier bytes from GetInfo.</param>
            <returns>Caller-owned plaintext, or null for empty/short input or a caught cryptographic failure.</returns>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The plaintext is a device identifier, not a credential ID. Randomized encryption changes the
            ciphertext on each GetInfo output; it does not make the decrypted identifier session-specific.
            No authenticity or correct-token check is performed. Clear the returned plaintext when done.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Crypto.EncryptedMetadataDecryptor.DecryptCredStoreState(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Decrypts the encCredStoreState field using PPUAT-derived key.
            </summary>
            <param name="ppuat">The Persistent PIN/UV Auth Token.</param>
            <param name="encCredStoreState">Borrowed IV-prefixed encCredStoreState bytes from GetInfo.</param>
            <returns>Caller-owned plaintext, or null for empty/short input or a caught cryptographic failure.</returns>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The plaintext describes opaque credential-store state, not an individual credential's metadata.
            No integer or status interpretation, authenticity check or correct-token check is performed.
            Clear the returned plaintext when done.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Crypto.EncryptedMetadataDecryptor.DeriveKey(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Derives an AES-128 key from PPUAT using HKDF-SHA256.
            </summary>
            <param name="ppuat">The Persistent PIN/UV Auth Token.</param>
            <param name="info">The context info string (e.g., "encIdentifier").</param>
            <returns>A caller-owned 16-byte secret AES key; clear it when finished, including on later failure.</returns>
            <remarks>
            This can be used for custom decryption scenarios. For standard 
            encIdentifier/encCredStoreState, prefer the specific decrypt methods.
            </remarks>
        </member>
