        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobAssertionOutput">
            <summary>
            Output from the credBlob extension during getAssertion.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Contains the blob data stored with the credential, if any.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobAssertionOutput.Blob">
            <summary>
            Gets the stored blob data.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            The blob data that was stored during makeCredential.
            Empty if no blob was stored; an empty byte string is distinct from an absent extension.
            Direct init borrows supplied storage; Decode creates an independent byte-array copy.
            Keep borrowed storage stable during use. This DTO has no disposal/zeroing boundary;
            disposing the session or clearing the source response does not clear that copy.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobAssertionOutput.Decode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Decodes credBlob output from a CBOR reader (getAssertion response).
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader.</param>
            <returns>The decoded output.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobInput">
            <summary>
            Input for the credBlob extension during makeCredential.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The credBlob extension allows storing a small blob of data with a credential.
            The authenticator advertises maxCredBlobLength and must support at least 32 bytes, not exactly
            32 bytes. This DTO currently restricts input to 1–32 bytes as an SDK limitation; the builder's
            WithCredBlob method has no corresponding size check.
            </para>
            <para>
            This is useful for storing small amounts of credential-specific data like:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>Account identifiers</description></item>
              <item><description>Configuration flags</description></item>
              <item><description>Small metadata</description></item>
            </list>
            </para>
            <para>
            For PII or other sensitive content, CTAP 2.1 §12.2 requires the RP to request
            UserVerificationRequired credential protection with enforcement enabled. ExtensionBuilder currently
            does not enforce that policy; check support before creation when prevention is required and inspect
            the returned protection policy. Post-creation inspection cannot undo creation.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#sctn-credBlob-extension
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobInput.Blob">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the blob data to store with the credential.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            This DTO accepts 1–32 bytes; that is an SDK restriction, not the protocol's maximum capacity.
            The memory is borrowed, not copied. Keep it unchanged through encoding and transmission,
            then clear caller-owned sensitive storage when it is no longer needed.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobInput.Encode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborWriter)">
            <summary>
            Encodes this credBlob input as CBOR (the raw blob bytes).
            </summary>
            <param name="writer">The CBOR writer.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobInput.Encode">
            <summary>
            Encodes this credBlob input as a CBOR byte array.
            </summary>
            <returns>A new caller-owned CBOR copy; clear it after use if the blob is sensitive.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobMakeCredentialOutput">
            <summary>
            Output from the credBlob extension during makeCredential.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Indicates whether the blob was successfully stored.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobMakeCredentialOutput.Stored">
            <summary>
            Gets whether the credBlob was successfully stored.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            True if the authenticator accepted and stored the blob.
            False if storage failed (e.g., blob too large).
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredBlobMakeCredentialOutput.Decode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Decodes credBlob output from a CBOR reader (makeCredential response).
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader.</param>
            <returns>The decoded output.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredProtectPolicy">
            <summary>
            Credential protection policy for the credProtect extension.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The credential protection policy specifies when credentials can be used
            in assertions. Higher values provide stronger protection but may limit
            compatibility with some relying parties.
            The requested policy is not proof of the effective policy: authenticators may return a stronger
            policy. ExtensionBuilder's enforcePolicy parameter currently has no effect. In CTAP 2.1 §12.1.1,
            enforcement for levels 2 and 3 is a platform SHOULD NOT creation rule, not an extra CTAP wire flag.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#sctn-credProtect-extension
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredProtectPolicy.UserVerificationOptional">
            <summary>
            User verification is optional.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Credentials can be discovered and used without user verification.
            CTAP 2.1 recommends this default when credProtect is omitted, but allows stronger device defaults.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredProtectPolicy.UserVerificationOptionalWithCredentialIdList">
            <summary>
            User verification is optional with credential ID list.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            For discoverable credentials, user verification is required if
            no credential ID is provided (i.e., when listing discoverable credentials).
            When a credential ID is provided in allowList, UV is optional.
            Do not infer the authenticator's default from the credential being discoverable.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredProtectPolicy.UserVerificationRequired">
            <summary>
            User verification is always required.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            The credential can only be used with user verification. Assertions
            without UV will fail. This provides the highest protection level.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretInput">
            <summary>
            Input parameters for the hmac-secret extension during getAssertion.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The hmac-secret extension allows relying parties to derive a secret value
            from a credential. This is useful for:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>Disk encryption keys</description></item>
              <item><description>Password manager vault keys</description></item>
              <item><description>Credential-scoped symmetric key derivation</description></item>
            </list>
            </para>
            <para>
            The authenticator creates random credential secrets, with separate verified and unverified
            variants. PINs and biometrics authorize use; they are not the source of those secrets. Repeatable
            output requires the same credential, salt and actual UV mode. hmac-secret does not support up:false.
            Salt authentication is separate from the ceremony's pinUvAuthParam over clientDataHash.
            </para>
            <para>
            This DTO borrows its dictionary and byte buffers until encoding/transmission completes. It does
            not validate capability advertisement, key-agreement coherence or protocol-specific lengths.
            Clear caller-owned sensitive inputs and encoded copies after use; the DTO has no cleanup owner.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#sctn-hmac-secret-extension
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretInput.KeyAgreement">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the platform's key agreement public key (COSE format).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            This is an ephemeral EC P-256 public key used for ECDH with the authenticator.
            Must be encoded as a COSE_Key.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretInput.SaltEnc">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the encrypted salt values.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Contains one or two 32-byte salts encrypted with the shared secret:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>Protocol 1: 32 bytes for one salt, 64 bytes for two; no IV prefix.</description></item>
              <item><description>Protocol 2: 48 bytes for one salt, 80 bytes for two; includes a 16-byte IV.</description></item>
            </list>
            </para>
            <para>
            For PIN protocol 2, the ciphertext includes the IV prefix.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretInput.SaltAuth">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the HMAC over the encrypted salts.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Computed as: authenticate(sharedSecret, saltEnc).
            For PIN protocol 1: first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA-256.
            For PIN protocol 2: full 32 bytes of HMAC-SHA-256.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretInput.PinUvAuthProtocol">
            <summary>
            Gets or sets the PIN/UV auth protocol version.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Must match the protocol used to compute keyAgreement, saltEnc, and saltAuth.
            Typical values: 1 or 2.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretInput.Encode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborWriter)">
            <summary>
            Encodes this hmac-secret input as CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="writer">The CBOR writer.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretInput.Encode">
            <summary>
            Encodes this hmac-secret input as a CBOR byte array.
            </summary>
            <returns>A new caller-owned CBOR copy of the encrypted salts and authentication material.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretOutput">
            <summary>
            Output from the hmac-secret extension during getAssertion.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Contains the encrypted derived secret(s). The client must decrypt using
            the shared secret established during key agreement.
            This byte-string shape is used for assertion output and hmac-secret-mc evaluation output,
            not the boolean hmac-secret registration support result. Decrypted output depends on the
            credential, salts and actual UV mode. Clear caller-owned shared secrets and plaintext after use.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretOutput.Output">
            <summary>
            Gets the encrypted output value(s).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Contains one or two 32-byte derived secrets, encrypted:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>Protocol 1: 32 bytes for one output, 64 bytes for two; no IV prefix.</description></item>
              <item><description>Protocol 2: 48 bytes for one output, 80 bytes for two; includes a 16-byte IV.</description></item>
            </list>
            </para>
            <para>
            For PIN protocol 2, includes the IV prefix (16 bytes).
            Direct init borrows supplied storage; keep it stable during use. Decode allocates an independent
            byte-array copy and does not validate these lengths.
            This DTO has no disposal/zeroing boundary; response or session disposal does not clear the copy.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretOutput.Decode(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Decodes hmac-secret output from CBOR bytes.
            </summary>
            <param name="data">The CBOR-encoded output.</param>
            <returns>The decoded output.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretOutput.Decode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Decodes hmac-secret output from a CBOR reader.
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader.</param>
            <returns>The decoded output.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.LargeBlobOutput">
            <summary>
            Legacy convenience container for key, blob and write-result values.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This decoder consumes a synthetic map with largeBlobKey, blob and written members; that combined
            shape is not a standard CTAP extension output. The implemented largeBlobKey/storage route returns
            keys on MakeCredentialResponse.LargeBlobKey or GetAssertionResponse.LargeBlobKey, outside authData
            extensions. CTAP 2.3 §12.4's alternative direct largeBlob route uses unsigned supported/read/write
            outputs and compressed blob plus originalSize, not this container or WebAuthn's decompressed result.
            This DTO performs no storage read, decompression, decryption or authenticity verification.
            Direct init borrows supplied memory; keep it stable during use. Decoded byte strings are
            independent copies with no disposal/zeroing boundary.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.LargeBlobOutput.LargeBlobKey">
            <summary>
            Gets the large blob key.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            A 32-byte key used to encrypt/decrypt large blob data for this credential.
            A key supplied to this container, not a guarantee about how an authenticator generated it.
            This is secret material, not public metadata; do not log or persist it unprotected.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.LargeBlobOutput.Blob">
            <summary>
            Gets blob bytes supplied to this convenience container, without a decryption guarantee.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            The container does not establish that these bytes were decrypted. Direct CTAP read output
            is compressed and also requires originalSize, which this DTO does not model. Use LargeBlobStorage
            for the implemented key/storage route; callers own plaintext returned by that helper.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.LargeBlobOutput.Written">
            <summary>
            Gets the supplied written value, without independently establishing a completed storage write.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Null means no written value was supplied or decoded. True and false reflect the supplied
            boolean, not a tracked request or independently established storage success.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.LargeBlobOutput.Decode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Decodes largeBlob output from a CBOR reader.
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader.</param>
            <returns>The decoded output.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.MinPinLengthInput">
            <summary>
            Input for the minPinLength extension during makeCredential.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The minPinLength extension allows a relying party to request the minimum PIN length
            currently required by the authenticator, in Unicode code points. It neither changes policy nor
            proves the current PIN's length or all complexity rules.
            </para>
            <para>
            During credential creation, the RP must be authorized by the authenticator's minPinLengthRPIDs
            configuration. An unauthorized RP receives no extension output, not a zero minimum.
            Use AuthenticatorConfig to change minimum-PIN policy; this input only requests disclosure.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#sctn-minPinLength-extension
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.MinPinLengthInput.Requested">
            <summary>
            Gets whether to request the minimum PIN length.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Set to true to request the minPinLength value from the authenticator.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.MinPinLengthInput.Encode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborWriter)">
            <summary>
            Encodes this minPinLength input as CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="writer">The CBOR writer.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.MinPinLengthInput.Encode">
            <summary>
            Encodes this minPinLength input as a CBOR byte array.
            </summary>
            <returns>The CBOR-encoded input.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.MinPinLengthOutput">
            <summary>
            Output from the minPinLength extension.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Reports the current minimum during credential creation for an authorized RP. Absence of output
            is not a zero minimum or proof the extension is unsupported.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.MinPinLengthOutput.MinPinLength">
            <summary>
            Gets the minimum PIN length in Unicode code points.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            The minimum number of Unicode code points required for a PIN.
            The preconfigured minimum is at least four code points. The separate 63-byte UTF-8 PIN limit
            is not this field's unit. Decode reads an Int32 without enforcing a 4–63 policy range.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.MinPinLengthOutput.Decode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Decodes minPinLength output from a CBOR reader.
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader.</param>
            <returns>The decoded output.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs">
            <summary>
            Experimental <c>COSE_Sign_Args</c> helper for ARKG-P256-ESP256 (alg = <c>-65539</c>). Wire shape:
            <c>{3: -65539, -1: kh, -2: ctx}</c>.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            <c>KeyHandle</c> is the 81-byte ARKG ciphertext (16-byte HMAC tag concatenated with a 65-byte
            SEC1 uncompressed-form ephemeral public key, leading <c>0x04</c>) returned by ARKG public-key
            derivation. <c>Context</c> is the HKDF context (≤64 bytes) bound to the derivation.
            </para>
            <para>
            <b>Memory ownership:</b> Both <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.KeyHandle"/> and <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.Context"/> are
            <see cref="T:System.ReadOnlyMemory`1"/> passthroughs — the encoder reads them at CBOR-write time
            without cloning the input into this record. Encoding nevertheless creates independent CBOR
            copies. Keep caller storage stable through encoding and awaited transmission, then clear it
            if application-sensitive. Neither this record nor its encoded copies have a disposal owner.
            </para>
            <para>
            <b>Algorithm identifier:</b> <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Cose.CoseAlgorithm.ArkgP256"/> (<c>-65539</c>) — this is
            the wire signing-op alg, not the seed-key COSE-key alg (<c>-65700</c>). See
            <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Cose.CoseAlgorithm.ArkgP256"/> XML doc for the full disambiguation.
            These are experimental profile identifiers, not production or full Internet-Draft conformance.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.ArkgTagLength">
            <summary>
            The 16-byte HMAC tag length within an ARKG-P256 key handle.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.Sec1UncompressedP256Length">
            <summary>
            The 65-byte SEC1 uncompressed P-256 point length (1-byte 0x04 prefix + 32-byte X + 32-byte Y).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.ArkgP256KeyHandleLength">
            <summary>
            Total ARKG-P256 key handle length: <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.ArkgTagLength"/> + <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.Sec1UncompressedP256Length"/> = 81.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.MaxContextLength">
            <summary>
            Maximum ARKG context length from draft-bradleylundberg-cfrg-arkg-10 §2.3's explicit algorithm bound,
            not the representable capacity of its one-byte length prefix.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.Algorithm">
            <summary>
            Algorithm identifier on the wire — fixed at <c>-65539</c>
            (<see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Cose.CoseAlgorithm.ArkgP256"/>).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.KeyHandle">
            <summary>
            The 81-byte ARKG-P256 key handle: 16-byte HMAC tag concatenated with 65-byte SEC1
            uncompressed ephemeral public key.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.Context">
            <summary>The ARKG context (≤64 bytes) bound to the derivation.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Initializes a new <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs"/> with the supplied key handle and context.
            </summary>
            <param name="keyHandle">The 81-byte ARKG-P256 key handle.</param>
            <param name="context">The ARKG HKDF context (0–64 bytes).</param>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">
            Thrown when <paramref name="keyHandle"/> is not exactly 81 bytes, or
            <paramref name="context"/> exceeds 64 bytes.
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs">
            <summary>
            Experimental typed helper for a <c>COSE_Sign_Args</c> map in the Yubico Labs previewSign v4 Editor's Draft.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            <c>COSE_Sign_Args</c> is a CBOR map whose key 3 carries the request algorithm identifier; the
            remaining keys are algorithm-specific. Today the only typed helper in this SDK is
            <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs"/> (alg = <c>-65539</c>).
            This is not CTAP version 4 or production cryptographic guidance. The helper borrows input buffers;
            encoding creates independent copies rather than a no-copy wire path.
            </para>
            <para>
            This helper is not the generic previewSign contract. Generic previewSign signing accepts raw
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams.AdditionalArgs"/> bytes. Use
            <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.EncodeAdditionalArgs(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs)"/> to convert this experimental typed helper
            to those raw bytes when testing ARKG flows in v2.
            </para>
            <para>
            This is a closed helper hierarchy: the constructor is <c>private protected</c>, so external
            assemblies cannot extend it. <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.EncodeCoseSignArgs(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs)"/> exhaustively
            pattern-matches the known subtypes and throws on unknown runtime types.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs.#ctor">
            <summary>
            Initializes a new instance of <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs"/>. <c>private protected</c>:
            only subtypes declared in this assembly may extend the hierarchy.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs.Algorithm">
            <summary>The COSE algorithm identifier written under key 3 of the <c>COSE_Sign_Args</c> map.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs.ArkgP256(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Experimental convenience factory: constructs an <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs"/> without naming the leaf type.
            </summary>
            <param name="keyHandle">The 81-byte ARKG key handle (16-byte HMAC tag concatenated with
            65-byte SEC1 uncompressed P-256 ephemeral public key).</param>
            <param name="context">The ARKG context (≤64 bytes) bound to the derivation.</param>
            <returns>A typed <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs"/>.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignAuthenticationOutput">
            <summary>
            Output from the previewSign extension authentication.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Contains signature bytes without verification. The Yubico Labs previewSign v4 Editor's Draft
            is experimental; algorithm-specific message hashing and signature format remain caller concerns.
            The constructor borrows storage, while PreviewSignCbor decoding creates an independent byte-string
            copy. Keep borrowed storage stable during use; this DTO has no disposal/zeroing boundary.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignAuthenticationOutput.Signature">
            <summary>
            Gets the signature bytes.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignAuthenticationOutput.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Initializes a new instance of <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignAuthenticationOutput"/>.
            </summary>
            <param name="signature">The signature bytes.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor">
            <summary>
            Encoding utilities for previewSign extension CBOR format.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            This is the canonical CBOR encoder for previewSign extension, shared by both
            CTAP2 and WebAuthn layers.
            The wire shape follows the Yubico Labs previewSign v4 Editor's Draft (26 August 2025),
            https://yubicolabs.github.io/webauthn-sign-extension/4/#sctn-sign-extension, not CTAP version 4.
            This is experimental, not production cryptographic guidance. Encoders read borrowed inputs and
            return independent arrays; they do not validate negotiation, attestation or algorithm-specific
            Tbs/args semantics. Decoded byte strings are copies without a disposable cleanup owner.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.RegistrationInputKeys">
            <summary>
            CBOR keys for registration input.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.AuthenticationInputKeys">
            <summary>
            CBOR keys for authentication input.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.RegistrationOutputKeys">
            <summary>
            CBOR keys for registration output.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.AuthenticationOutputKeys">
            <summary>
            CBOR keys for authentication output.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.CoseSignArgsKeys">
            <summary>
            CBOR keys inside a <c>COSE_Sign_Args</c> map.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Key 3 (alg) is the request signing-op algorithm; algorithm-specific payload
            keys live in negative integer space (-1, -2, ...). For ARKG-P256:
            <c>-1 = arkg_kh</c>, <c>-2 = ctx</c>.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.EncodeCoseSignArgs(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs)">
            <summary>
            Encodes a typed <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs"/> as CTAP2-canonical CBOR. The returned bytes
            are suitable for <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams.AdditionalArgs"/> and are wrapped
            unchanged as a CBOR byte-string under authentication input key 7.
            </summary>
            <param name="args">The typed <c>COSE_Sign_Args</c> value to encode.</param>
            <returns>CTAP2-canonical CBOR bytes for the <c>COSE_Sign_Args</c> map.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentNullException">Thrown when <paramref name="args"/> is null.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentOutOfRangeException">
            Thrown when the runtime <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs"/> subtype is not supported by this SDK
            build. Forward-compat trap: if a future Yubico-internal subtype is added without an
            encoder branch here, the call fails fast rather than silently emitting empty bytes.
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.EncodeAdditionalArgs(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs)">
            <summary>
            Encodes a typed <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs"/> helper into raw previewSign <c>additionalArgs</c> bytes.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            This is an experimental v2 convenience bridge for ARKG and other typed helpers. The generic
            previewSign signing API accepts raw <c>additionalArgs</c> bytes and does not require callers
            to use typed ARKG helpers.
            </remarks>
            <param name="args">The typed algorithm-specific signing arguments to encode.</param>
            <returns>Raw bytes suitable for <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams.AdditionalArgs"/>.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.EncodeArkgP256SignArgs(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs)">
            <summary>
            Encodes an <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ArkgP256SignArgs"/> as the 3-key CBOR map
            <c>{3: -65539, -1: kh, -2: ctx}</c> in CTAP2-canonical order.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            For these one-byte keys the canonical encoded order is 3, -1, -2. Ctap2Canonical supplies
            ordering at map completion. This experimental signing-op profile is not proof of full ARKG
            draft conformance; encoded output is a new copy of the supplied handle/context.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.EncodeRegistrationInput(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationInput)">
            <summary>
            Encodes registration input (algorithm list + flags) as canonical CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="input">The registration input.</param>
            <returns>CBOR-encoded map with keys {3: [alg...], 4: flags}.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.EncodeAuthenticationInput(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams)">
            <summary>
            Encodes authentication input for a single chosen credential as canonical CBOR.
            </summary>
            <param name="signingParams">The signing parameters for the chosen credential.</param>
            <returns>
            CBOR-encoded flat map {2: kh, 6: tbs, 7?: args} for the single credential.
            </returns>
            <remarks>
            Per Yubico Labs previewSign v4 §10.2.1, the client sends the chosen credential's params as a flat map:
            - 2 (kh): key handle (bstr)
            - 6 (tbs): to-be-signed data (bstr)
            - 7 (args): optional additional args wrapped as bstr (omitted if null)
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.DecodeRegistrationOutput(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Decodes registration output from authData.extensions["previewSign"].
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">CBOR reader positioned at the start of the previewSign output map.</param>
            <returns>
            The chosen algorithm and a nullable outer flags value accepted by this parser.
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException">
            Thrown when the required algorithm is missing. CBOR shape/content failures can throw CborContentException.
            </exception>
            <remarks>
            The v4 Editor's Draft signed outer output has algorithm key 3 only; policy flags belong inside
            the signing-key attestation. This parser tolerates outer key 4 but its absence is not a
            beta-firmware exception or evidence about the inner policy. Parsing does not verify the signature.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.InnerAttestationObjectKeys">
            <summary>
            CBOR keys inside the previewSign nested attestation object (CTAP-shaped, integer-keyed).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            The previewSign unsigned-extension-output payload wraps an inner attestation object whose
            keys are CTAP-style integers ({1:fmt, 2:authData, 3:attStmt}), NOT WebAuthn-style text
            strings ({"fmt","authData","attStmt"}). The Yubico Labs v4 draft wraps the encoded inner map
            in a byte string; this shape alone is not attestation verification or device qualification.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.InnerAttestationObject">
            <summary>
            Decoded components of the inner attestation object embedded in
            unsignedExtensionOutputs["previewSign"][7].
            </summary>
            <param name="Fmt">Attestation format identifier (e.g. "none", "packed").</param>
            <param name="AuthData">An independently decoded copy of CTAP authenticator-data bytes.</param>
            <param name="AttStmtRawCbor">Slice of the decoded inner-map storage; not a complete original response. Decode and verify with the appropriate format/policy.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.InnerAttestationObject.#ctor(System.String,System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Decoded components of the inner attestation object embedded in
            unsignedExtensionOutputs["previewSign"][7].
            </summary>
            <param name="Fmt">Attestation format identifier (e.g. "none", "packed").</param>
            <param name="AuthData">An independently decoded copy of CTAP authenticator-data bytes.</param>
            <param name="AttStmtRawCbor">Slice of the decoded inner-map storage; not a complete original response. Decode and verify with the appropriate format/policy.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.InnerAttestationObject.Fmt">
            <summary>Attestation format identifier (e.g. "none", "packed").</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.InnerAttestationObject.AuthData">
            <summary>An independently decoded copy of CTAP authenticator-data bytes.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.InnerAttestationObject.AttStmtRawCbor">
            <summary>Slice of the decoded inner-map storage; not a complete original response. Decode and verify with the appropriate format/policy.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.DecodeUnsignedRegistrationOutput(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Decodes unsigned registration output from unsignedExtensionOutputs["previewSign"].
            </summary>
            <param name="cbor">CBOR outer map with key 7 containing a byte string of encoded inner-attestation CBOR.</param>
            <returns>
            The decoded inner attestation object components (fmt, authData, attStmt raw CBOR).
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException">
            Thrown when required fields are missing. CBOR content/type failures can throw CborContentException.
            </exception>
            <remarks>
            Per the Yubico Labs previewSign v4 Editor's Draft, unsigned output contains key 7 (att-obj), a byte string wrapping a CTAP-shaped
            attestation object map {1:fmt, 2:authData, 3:attStmt}. NOTE: the inner map uses integer
            keys (not the WebAuthn text-string keys "fmt"/"authData"/"attStmt"). Callers that need a
            WebAuthn-spec attestation object must rebuild it from these components rather than feeding
            the inner CBOR directly to a WebAuthn decoder.
            These components are parsed, not verified; validate attestation, chosen algorithm, key binding
            and inner policy before trust. The copied inner map/authData have no disposal/zeroing owner.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.DecodeInnerAttestationObject(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Decodes the CTAP-shaped inner attestation object: {1:fmt, 2:authData, 3:attStmt}.
            Captures the raw CBOR slice for attStmt so callers can route it to a format-specific decoder.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.DecodeAuthenticationOutput(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Decodes authentication output from authData.extensions["previewSign"].
            </summary>
            <param name="cbor">CBOR-encoded map with key {6: sig}.</param>
            <returns>
            The signature bytes.
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException">
            Thrown when signature is missing. CBOR content/type failures can throw CborContentException.
            </exception>
            <remarks>
            Per Yubico Labs previewSign v4 §10.2.1, key 6 contains the signature. The returned byte string
            is an independent copy; this does not verify the signature or its algorithm-specific format.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.TryExtractGeneratedKey(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialResponse,Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey@)">
            <summary>
            Attempts to extract a typed <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey"/> from a
            MakeCredential response that includes the previewSign extension.
            </summary>
            <param name="response">The MakeCredential response.</param>
            <param name="generatedKey">
            When this method returns <c>true</c>, contains the extracted generated key;
            otherwise, <c>null</c>.
            </param>
            <returns>
            <c>true</c> if syntactic extraction yields the SDK's experimental ARKG-P256 seed-key carrier;
            otherwise, <c>false</c>.
            </returns>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Parses unsignedExtensionOutputs["previewSign"], extracts the inner attested credential data
            and decodes its COSE seed-key carrier. It does not verify attestation, device identity,
            signed algorithm agreement, generated-key binding or inner UP/UV policy.
            </para>
            <para>
            Returns false for absent output/attested data, another key carrier, or caught CborContentException
            and InvalidOperationException. Other malformed-authData failures, such as ArgumentException,
            can propagate. The returned convenience object has no disposal owner and uses the seed's derived
            algorithm, unlike PreviewSignRegistrationOutput.TryGetGeneratedKey's current seed-marker propagation.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey">
            <summary>
            Represents a derived public key produced by ARKG-P256 derivation.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            <b>WARNING -- EXPERIMENTAL --</b> ARKG previewSign derived-key helpers are not ready for production use and
            must not be treated as production cryptographic guidance.
            </para>
            <para>
            This class contains the derived public key and handles needed for the
            ESP256-split-ARKG previewSign helper path. Instances are obtained
            by calling <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey.DerivePublicKey(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})"/> with
            application-provided input keying material and a context string.
            </para>
            <para>
            The derived public key can be used to verify signatures produced by the
            YubiKey when signing with the corresponding ARKG key handle and context.
            Use <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.VerifySignature(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})"/> to validate signatures against this key.
            </para>
            <para>
            To request a signature from the YubiKey using this derived key, pass the
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.DeviceKeyHandle"/>, <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.ArkgKeyHandle"/>, and
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.Context"/> properties to the previewSign authentication extension input.
            Memory properties retain their supplied storage. The derivation helper supplies new point/ARKG
            handle/context arrays but borrows the original device handle. There is no disposable cleanup
            owner. Public points are not secrets; application-sensitive contexts/handles need caller policy.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.PublicKey">
            <summary>
            Gets the derived public key (65-byte SEC1 uncompressed point).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.ArkgKeyHandle">
            <summary>
            Gets the ARKG key handle.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.DeviceKeyHandle">
            <summary>
            Gets the device key handle from the original registration.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.Context">
            <summary>
            Gets the context string used for derivation.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Initializes a new instance of the <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey"/> class.
            </summary>
            <param name="publicKey">The derived public key (65-byte SEC1 uncompressed point).</param>
            <param name="arkgKeyHandle">The ARKG key handle.</param>
            <param name="deviceKeyHandle">The device key handle.</param>
            <param name="context">The context string.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.VerifySignature(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Verifies a signature against the derived public key.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            <b>WARNING -- EXPERIMENTAL --</b> This ARKG signature-verification helper is not ready for production use
            and must not be treated as production cryptographic guidance.
            </para>
            <para>
            This helper always imports P-256 and hashes the raw message with SHA-256; it is not an
            algorithm-agile verifier or attestation/RP verification. Passing an already-hashed Tbs value
            hashes it again. Match the experimental signing operation's Tbs convention to this raw-message API.
            </para>
            <para>
            The signature must be in DER-encoded ECDSA format, as returned by the
            YubiKey's previewSign extension. The message should be the original raw data,
            not a pre-hashed value.
            The current DER converter reads two INTEGERs without checking complete sequence/root consumption
            or all positive/canonical component conditions. Do not rely on it as strict DER validation.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <param name="message">
            The message that was signed. This method will hash the message internally
            before verifying the signature.
            </param>
            <param name="signature">
            The DER-encoded ESP256-split-ARKG previewSign signature to verify.
            </param>
            <returns>
            <c>true</c> if the signature is valid for the message using the derived
            public key under this fixed P-256/SHA-256 helper; also false for caught parsing/crypto errors.
            </returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey">
            <summary>
            Represents the generated key material returned by the YubiKey during
            previewSign extension registration.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            <b>WARNING -- EXPERIMENTAL --</b> ARKG previewSign derivation helpers are not ready for production use and
            must not be treated as production cryptographic guidance.
            </para>
            <para>
            This class contains the key handle and public key components needed to
            perform RP-side ARKG-P256 public key derivation via <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey.DerivePublicKey(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})"/>.
            </para>
            <para>
            Instances of this class are obtained by calling
            <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput.TryGetGeneratedKey"/> after creating
            a credential with the previewSign extension enabled.
            </para>
            <para>
            The public seed permits offline derivations using input keying material and a context. It is not
            proof of attestation, device identity, key binding or uniqueness for every different context.
            Memory supplied to this object is borrowed; derived points/handles and copied contexts have no
            disposal owner. Public points are not secrets, but application-sensitive context/handle storage
            should not be logged and must follow the application's lifetime policy.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey.KeyHandle">
            <summary>
            Gets the key handle used to request signatures from this generated signing key.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey.BlindingPublicKey">
            <summary>
            Gets the blinding public key component.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey.KemPublicKey">
            <summary>
            Gets the KEM public key component.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey.DerivedKeyAlgorithm">
            <summary>
            Gets the algorithm identifier for the derived key.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Extraction paths currently disagree: TryGetGeneratedKey supplies seed marker -65700, while
            PreviewSignCbor.TryExtractGeneratedKey supplies the seed's derived algorithm (typically -9).
            DerivePublicKey does not dispatch on this property; its verifier is fixed to P-256/SHA-256.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Cose.CoseAlgorithm)">
            <summary>
            Initializes a new instance of the <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey"/> class.
            </summary>
            <param name="keyHandle">The key handle.</param>
            <param name="blindingPublicKey">The blinding public key.</param>
            <param name="kemPublicKey">The KEM public key.</param>
            <param name="derivedKeyAlgorithm">The derived key algorithm.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey.DerivePublicKey(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Derives a public key using the ARKG-P256 algorithm.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            <b>WARNING -- EXPERIMENTAL --</b> This ARKG derivation helper is not ready for production use and must not
            be treated as production cryptographic guidance.
            </para>
            <para>
            This method performs offline key derivation using the ARKG-P256 algorithm.
            The derived public key can be used to verify signatures created by the
            YubiKey when provided with the corresponding ARKG key handle and context.
            </para>
            <para>
            Different input keying material/context values provide derivation/domain-separation inputs;
            this helper does not establish unconditional uniqueness or full conformance to the cited ARKG
            Internet-Draft. Context is limited to 64 bytes by the experimental algorithm's explicit bound.
            </para>
            <para>
            To request an ESP256-split-ARKG signature with this helper, pass the returned
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.DeviceKeyHandle"/>,
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.ArkgKeyHandle"/>, and
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.Context"/> to the previewSign authentication extension input.
            The YubiKey will produce a signature that can be verified using
            <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey.VerifySignature(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})"/>.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <param name="ikm">
            Input keying material for HKDF derivation. This should be random data
            unique to the derivation context.
            </param>
            <param name="ctx">
            Borrowed context bytes for domain separation (0–64 bytes); copied into the returned result.
            </param>
            <returns>
            A <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignDerivedKey"/> containing the derived public key,
            ARKG key handle, device key handle, and context.
            </returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationInput">
            <summary>
            Input for the previewSign extension registration (key generation).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The previewSign extension allows a CTAP2 credential to sign arbitrary data using a separate
            signing key bound to the same authenticator. This input specifies the acceptable signing
            algorithms for registration (key generation).
            </para>
            <para>
            See https://yubicolabs.github.io/webauthn-sign-extension/4/#sctn-sign-extension:
            Yubico Labs previewSign version 4, Editor's Draft of 26 August 2025, not CTAP version 4.
            This preview and its algorithms/identifiers may change; do not use it as production guidance.
            The algorithms list is borrowed until encoding/transmission completes. The constructor checks a
            nonempty list, but init properties can replace values and the encoder does not validate flags,
            algorithm support or ceremony policy.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationInput.Algorithms">
            <summary>
            Gets the ordered list of acceptable COSE algorithms, from most to least preferred.
            The authenticator will select the first algorithm it supports.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationInput.Flags">
            <summary>
            Gets the user presence and verification policy for signing operations.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Draft policies: 0 = unattended, 0x01 = UP required, 0x05 = UP and UV required.
            The constructor defaults to 0x01 and the encoder always sends this property. The device's
            signing policy is fixed at key generation; a later request cannot relax it.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationInput.#ctor(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList{System.Int32},System.Byte)">
            <summary>
            Initializes a new instance of <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationInput"/>.
            </summary>
            <param name="algorithms">Ordered list of COSE algorithm identifiers.</param>
            <param name="flags">User presence/verification flags (default: 0x01).</param>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput">
            <summary>
            Output from the previewSign extension registration.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Contains experimental generated signing-key information, not verified attestation or device identity.
            The signed outer previewSign output carries the chosen algorithm; the unsigned wrapped signing-key
            attestation carries the generated key and inner signing policy. Verify attestation/key binding and
            policy before trusting it. The constructor borrows memory; decoders may allocate independent copies.
            This DTO supplies no disposal/zeroing boundary.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput.KeyHandle">
            <summary>
            Gets the key handle of the generated signing key.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput.PublicKey">
            <summary>
            Gets the COSE public key of the generated signing key.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput.Algorithm">
            <summary>
            Gets the COSE algorithm identifier of the generated key.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput.AttestationObject">
            <summary>
            Gets the attestation object containing the signing key.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            May be null if authenticator did not provide unsigned extension outputs.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Int32,System.Nullable{System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte}})">
            <summary>
            Initializes a new instance of <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput"/>.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput.TryGetGeneratedKey">
            <summary>
            Attempts to extract a typed <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey"/> from the
            registration output.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This method decodes the <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationOutput.PublicKey"/> CBOR and returns a
            <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey"/> if the key is an ARKG-P256 seed-key
            (COSE_Key with alg -65700). Returns <c>null</c> if the public key is not
            an ARKG seed-key variant.
            </para>
            <para>
            This is syntactic extraction, not attestation verification. The raw PublicKey remains available.
            Currently this accessor propagates the seed-key marker (-65700) into DerivedKeyAlgorithm,
            unlike PreviewSignCbor.TryExtractGeneratedKey, which propagates the derived algorithm (-9 in
            the P-256 profile). Do not treat those algorithm properties as interchangeable or validated
            negotiation. The signing-operation identifier (-65539) has a third, distinct role.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <returns>
            A <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignGeneratedKey"/> if the public key is an ARKG-P256 seed-key;
            otherwise, <c>null</c>.
            </returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams">
            <summary>
            Parameters for signing arbitrary data with a previewSign credential.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Specifies the key handle, data to be signed, and optional algorithm-specific arguments
            for a single signing operation.
            </para>
            <para>
            The parameters correspond to the <c>keyHandle</c>, <c>tbs</c>, and optional
            <c>additionalArgs</c> fields of the previewSign signing input dictionary.
            The <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams.Tbs"/> and <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams.AdditionalArgs"/> values are algorithm-specific
            signing inputs and are encoded unchanged.
            Pass <c>null</c> to omit key 7. Passing an empty memory value emits key 7 with an empty
            byte string, matching the caller-supplied algorithm-specific value.
            Experimental typed helpers such as <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs"/> can be converted to raw
            <c>additionalArgs</c> bytes with <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignCbor.EncodeAdditionalArgs(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CoseSignArgs)"/>.
            The Yubico Labs previewSign v4 Editor's Draft requires present additionalArgs to encode a
            COSE_Sign_Args CBOR map; this passthrough does not validate that requirement. An empty byte
            string is emitted unchanged but is not thereby valid for every algorithm. Tbs may be raw data
            or a digest depending on the selected algorithm; the encoder does not hash it.
            </para>
            <para>
            Inputs are borrowed until encoding and awaited transmission complete; keep storage unchanged.
            Encoders make independent copies without a disposable cleanup owner. Clear caller-owned
            application-sensitive data after use. This preview is experimental and not production guidance.
            The constructor's nonempty keyHandle/Tbs guards are SDK restrictions, not universal draft rules
            (the draft permits an empty handle); init properties can replace the checked values.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams.KeyHandle">
            <summary>
            Gets the key handle from registration output.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams.Tbs">
            <summary>
            Gets the algorithm-specific to-be-signed bytes, which may already be a digest.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams.AdditionalArgs">
            <summary>
            Gets the optional algorithm-specific <c>additionalArgs</c> value.
            When present, including when empty, the encoder emits these bytes unchanged under
            authentication input key 7. A <c>null</c> value omits key 7.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Nullable{System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte}})">
            <summary>
            Initializes a new instance of <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams"/>.
            </summary>
            <param name="keyHandle">The key handle for the signing key.</param>
            <param name="tbs">Data to be signed.</param>
            <param name="additionalArgs">Optional algorithm-specific <c>additionalArgs</c> value.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder">
            <summary>
            Builder for constructing CTAP2 extension input maps.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This builder creates the CBOR-encoded extensions map used in makeCredential
            and getAssertion requests. Extensions are added using the fluent API and
            encoded to CBOR when Build() is called.
            The builder retains borrowed inputs; keep their storage unchanged through the last Encode/Build
            that reads them. Build creates an independent encoded copy; retain that encoded map/request through
            awaited transmission. Clearing inputs does not clear the copy, which has no disposable owner.
            The builder does not negotiate capabilities or generally validate ceremony/protocol coherence.
            Helper-generated salt buffers and authentication copies are not comprehensively cleared by this builder.
            </para>
            <para>
            Composable registration fragment with an existing ReadOnlyMemory&lt;byte&gt; myBlobData within the
            authenticator's maxCredBlobLength. For sensitive content, check credProtect support before creation
            and enforce level 3 in the application; this builder does not implement enforcement.
            <code>
            var extensions = new ExtensionBuilder()
                .WithCredProtect(CredProtectPolicy.UserVerificationRequired)
                .WithCredBlob(myBlobData)
                .Build();
            </code>
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithCredProtect(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredProtectPolicy,System.Boolean)">
            <summary>
            Adds the credProtect extension with the specified policy.
            </summary>
            <param name="policy">The credential protection policy.</param>
            <param name="enforcePolicy">Currently recorded but not enforced by the SDK; has no effect on encoding or creation.</param>
            <remarks>
            CTAP 2.1 §12.1.1 says the platform SHOULD NOT create a credential without requested level-2/3
            protection when enforcement is requested. This is not an authenticator wire flag. Check support
            before creation if prevention is required and inspect the effective returned policy, which may
            be stronger than requested. Rejecting a result afterward does not undo creation.
            </remarks>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithCredBlob(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Adds the credBlob extension with data to store (authenticatorMakeCredential only).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            CTAP 2.1-2.3 §12.2.1: the makeCredential input is a "Byte String containing the credBlob value".
            To read a stored blob back at getAssertion use <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithGetCredBlob"/>; a byte string is
            not the getAssertion input.
            This builder does not check size or capability. A supporting authenticator advertises
            maxCredBlobLength of at least 32 bytes. For PII/sensitive content the RP MUST request level-3
            credProtect with enforcement; the SDK currently leaves enforcement to the application.
            </remarks>
            <param name="blob">The blob data to store (at most the authenticator's maxCredBlobLength).</param>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithGetCredBlob">
            <summary>
            Requests the stored credBlob (authenticatorGetAssertion only).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            CTAP 2.1-2.3 §12.2.1: the platform sends <c>"credBlob": true</c> in the getAssertion extensions
            when the relying party set the <c>getCredBlob</c> client input.
            </remarks>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithLargeBlobKey">
            <summary>
            Adds the largeBlobKey CTAP extension for makeCredential or getAssertion.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This is the CTAP-level extension ("largeBlobKey": true) that instructs the
            authenticator to return a 32-byte large blob key with the credential response.
            This key is then used to encrypt/decrypt data in the large blob array.
            </para>
            <para>
            WebAuthn's <c>largeBlob</c> client extension ({support}, read, write; L3 §10.1.5) is built on this
            key in the WebAuthn package together with <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage"/> (§6.10).
            This builder's route sends no <c>largeBlob: {support}</c>. The direct largeBlob registration
            and assertion extension of CTAP 2.2-2.3 §12.4 does define support/read/write inputs and is a
            mutually exclusive alternative to largeBlobKey (§12.4:
            authenticators "MUST NOT support both extensions") and is not offered by this builder.
            Check largeBlobKey advertisement and largeBlobs:true; creation requires a discoverable credential
            (rk:true). Read the key from the credential response envelope, not its signed extensions map.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithHmacSecret">
            <summary>
            Requests hmac-secret at authenticatorMakeCredential: <c>"hmac-secret": true</c>
            (CTAP 2.1 §12.5; CTAP 2.2-2.3 §12.7).
            WebAuthn's prf extension (L3 §10.1.4) sends this at registration.
            </summary>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithHmacSecret(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretInput)">
            <summary>
            Adds the hmac-secret extension for getAssertion.
            </summary>
            <param name="input">The hmac-secret input parameters.</param>
            <remarks>Input is borrowed until encoding. Capability and protocol coherence remain caller responsibilities.</remarks>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithHmacSecret(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol,System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.Int32,System.Object},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Adds the hmac-secret extension for getAssertion using protocol helpers.
            </summary>
            <param name="protocol">The PIN/UV auth protocol.</param>
            <param name="sharedSecret">The shared secret from key agreement.</param>
            <param name="keyAgreement">The platform's key agreement public key.</param>
            <param name="salt1">The first salt (32 bytes).</param>
            <param name="salt2">Optional second salt (32 bytes). Pass empty span for no second salt.</param>
            <remarks>
            Use a mutually supported protocol and its matching encapsulated shared secret (32 bytes for
            protocol 1, 64 for protocol 2), not a PIN token. Encrypted salts are 32/64 bytes for protocol 1
            or 48/80 bytes including the IV for protocol 2; saltAuth is 16/32 bytes respectively.
            The helper reads spans during this call, retains the public dictionary and creates encrypted
            copies. It does not clear all plaintext/intermediate copies, including failure paths.
            Keep borrowed dictionary storage stable until encoding and clear caller-owned secrets after use.
            Actual UV mode selects the credential-secret variant; hmac-secret does not support up:false.
            </remarks>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.BuildHmacSecretInput(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol,System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.Int32,System.Object},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>CTAP 2.1 §12.5 / 2.2-2.3 §12.7: encrypt salts, then authenticate saltEnc with the same shared secret.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithHmacSecretMakeCredential(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretInput)">
            <summary>
            Adds the hmac-secret-mc extension (CTAP 2.2-2.3 §12.8): evaluate hmac-secret during
            authenticatorMakeCredential.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            §12.8: "This extension input is the same as the hmac secret extension's getAssertion input" and
            "the hmac-secret extension MUST also be present with the value of "hmac-secret" set to true", so
            this method also emits <c>"hmac-secret": true</c>. Check hmac-secret-mc advertisement on the actual
            authenticator; firmware alone is not capability evidence. Use raw hmac-secret-mc output with
            HmacSecretOutput.Decode; TryGetHmacSecret only addresses the hmac-secret key's assertion shape.
            </remarks>
            <param name="input">The encrypted and authenticated salts, as for getAssertion.</param>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithHmacSecretMakeCredential(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol,System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.Int32,System.Object},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Adds the hmac-secret-mc extension (CTAP 2.2-2.3 §12.8), encrypting the salts under the shared
            secret exactly as <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithHmacSecret(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol,System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.Int32,System.Object},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})"/> does.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithMinPinLength">
            <summary>
            Requests disclosure of the current minimum PIN length during credential creation.
            </summary>
            <remarks>Only authorized minPinLengthRPIDs receive output, in Unicode code points. This does not set PIN policy.</remarks>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithPreviewSign(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignRegistrationInput)">
            <summary>
            Adds previewSign extension with key generation parameters for makeCredential.
            </summary>
            <param name="input">The previewSign registration input.</param>
            <remarks>
            Experimental Yubico Labs previewSign v4 Editor's Draft input, not CTAP version 4 or production
            cryptographic guidance. Add only the input for this ceremony. If both overloads are used,
            this builder currently emits registration input and ignores signing input.
            </remarks>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.WithPreviewSign(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.PreviewSignSigningParams)">
            <summary>
            Adds the previewSign extension for getAssertion: the signing parameters of the one credential
            this assertion is for (Yubico previewSign draft v4 §10.2.1: key-handle, tbs, additional-args).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            CTAP carries exactly one credential's parameters. Choosing among a relying party's per-credential
            map (<c>signByCredential</c>) is the WebAuthn client's job, after it has selected the credential.
            Use a nonempty allow list for the selected credential and only this ceremony's previewSign input.
            The builder does not validate selection or algorithm-specific arguments. The Yubico Labs v4
            Editor's Draft is experimental, not a CTAP version or production cryptographic guidance.
            </remarks>
            <param name="signingParams">The selected credential's signing parameters.</param>
            <returns>This builder for chaining.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.Build">
            <summary>
            Builds the CBOR-encoded extensions map.
            </summary>
            <returns>An independent encoded copy, or null if no extensions. No disposal/zeroing owner is provided.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionBuilder.Encode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborWriter)">
            <summary>
            Encodes the extensions map to a CBOR writer.
            </summary>
            <param name="writer">The CBOR writer.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionIdentifiers">
            <summary>
            Identifiers for modeled CTAP extensions and the experimental Yubico Labs previewSign extension.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#sctn-defined-extensions
            That revision defines the base extensions, not hmac-secret-mc or previewSign. hmac-secret-mc is
            defined in CTAP 2.2-2.3 §12.8. previewSign uses the separate Yubico Labs v4 Editor's Draft.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionIdentifiers.HmacSecret">
            <summary>
            The hmac-secret extension identifier.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Allows deriving a secret value from a credential during assertions.
            Useful for disk encryption, password managers, etc.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionIdentifiers.HmacSecretMakeCredential">
            <summary>
            The hmac-secret-mc extension identifier (during makeCredential).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Evaluates hmac-secret during credential creation (CTAP 2.2-2.3 §12.8), returning encrypted
            output. Requires separate advertisement and hmac-secret:true in the same request.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionIdentifiers.CredProtect">
            <summary>
            The credProtect extension identifier.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Specifies the credential protection policy, controlling when
            user verification is required.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionIdentifiers.CredBlob">
            <summary>
            The credBlob extension identifier.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Allows storing a small blob of data (up to maxCredBlobLength bytes)
            along with the credential. Retrieved during assertions.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionIdentifiers.LargeBlob">
            <summary>
            The largeBlob extension identifier.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            CTAP 2.3 §12.4's direct storage alternative: registration requests support; assertion requests
            read/write. Outputs are unsigned, with compressed read data plus originalSize. This route is
            not implemented by ExtensionBuilder/LargeBlobStorage and is distinct from WebAuthn output.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionIdentifiers.LargeBlobKey">
            <summary>
            The largeBlobKey extension identifier.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Requests the credential's secret storage key for use with authenticatorLargeBlobs (§6.10).
            Returned at makeCredential key 5 or getAssertion key 7, not in authData extensions (§12.3).
            Check largeBlobKey advertisement and largeBlobs:true; it is mutually exclusive with direct largeBlob.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionIdentifiers.MinPinLength">
            <summary>
            The minPinLength extension identifier.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Returns the minimum PIN length required by the authenticator.
            Requested during makeCredential for an authorized RP; reports Unicode code points without
            changing policy or attesting all PIN complexity rules.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionIdentifiers.PreviewSign">
            <summary>
            The experimental previewSign identifier (Yubico Labs version 4 Editor's Draft, 26 August 2025).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Allows a CTAP2 credential to sign arbitrary data using a separate
            signing key bound to the same authenticator. Registration generates
            a new signing key pair; authentication signs data without clientDataJSON
            or authenticator data wrapping.
            See https://yubicolabs.github.io/webauthn-sign-extension/4/#sctn-sign-extension.
            This is not CTAP version 4. Preview algorithms and identifiers may change; do not use in production.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput">
            <summary>
            Parser for CTAP2 extension output maps.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This convenience parser expects a definite-length authData extensions map, not the complete CTAP response or
            unsigned extension outputs. The memory overload reconstructs supported values into new CBOR arrays;
            it does not preserve byte-exact original encoding or every valid unknown CBOR value. Supported
            values are signed-range integers, byte/text strings, booleans, null, arrays and maps of those values.
            Tags, floats and other simple values can be lost or cause reconstruction failure; large unsigned
            integers can fail. Duplicate identifiers overwrite earlier values. Retain the source parent raw
            response/authenticator-data bytes when exact or unknown data is needed; their guarantees are separate.
            </para>
            <para>
            Reconstructed values and byte-string getters allocate independent copies with no disposal/zeroing
            boundary. Session disposal or clearing the source does not clear those copies. Typed Try methods
            are shape-specific, may reject present values, and can throw for malformed/wrong-shape input.
            </para>
            <para>
            Composable fragment with existing nonempty ReadOnlyMemory&lt;byte&gt; extensionCbor from authData:
            <code>
            var output = ExtensionOutput.Decode(extensionCbor);
            if (output.TryGetCredProtect(out var policy))
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Credential protection: {policy}");
            }
            </code>
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.HasExtensions">
            <summary>
            Gets whether this output contains any extensions.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.ExtensionIds">
            <summary>
            Gets the extension identifiers present in this output.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.TryGetCredProtect(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.CredProtectPolicy@)">
            <summary>
            Attempts to get the credProtect extension output.
            </summary>
            <param name="policy">The credential protection policy.</param>
            <returns>True for a decoded policy in range 1–3; false for absence or an out-of-range integer.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.TryGetCredBlobStored(System.Boolean@)">
            <summary>
            Attempts to get the credBlob extension output (makeCredential response).
            </summary>
            <param name="stored">Whether the blob was successfully stored.</param>
            <returns>True for a boolean storage result, including false; false for absence or another value shape.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.TryGetCredBlob(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte}@)">
            <summary>
            Attempts to get the credBlob extension output (getAssertion response).
            </summary>
            <param name="blob">An independent byte-array copy, possibly empty; no cleanup owner is provided.</param>
            <returns>True for a byte-string result, including an empty stored-blob result; false for absence or another shape.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.TryGetHmacSecret(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.HmacSecretOutput@)">
            <summary>
            Decodes encrypted assertion output at the hmac-secret key.
            </summary>
            <param name="output">The encrypted hmac-secret output.</param>
            <remarks>
            Not a registration-support accessor: hmac-secret's registration boolean causes a decoding error.
            For hmac-secret-mc, use TryGetRawExtension with its identifier and HmacSecretOutput.Decode.
            Decode the registration boolean explicitly from its raw value instead.
            </remarks>
            <returns>True if the extension was present.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.TryGetLargeBlob(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.LargeBlobOutput@)">
            <summary>
            Decodes the legacy convenience largeBlob value, not standard direct CTAP output.
            </summary>
            <param name="output">The largeBlob output.</param>
            <remarks>
            A boolean is mapped to Written; a map is passed to LargeBlobOutput.Decode. Neither establishes
            standard registration support or a completed storage write. CTAP direct largeBlob outputs are
            unsigned and require different modeling; the implemented key/storage route uses envelope keys.
            </remarks>
            <returns>True if the extension was present.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.TryGetLargeBlobKey(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte}@)">
            <summary>
            Looks for a largeBlobKey in legacy convenience extension data.
            </summary>
            <param name="key">The large blob key.</param>
            <remarks>
            Standard CTAP largeBlobKey has no authData extension output. Use MakeCredentialResponse.LargeBlobKey
            or GetAssertionResponse.LargeBlobKey instead. This method's copied secret has no cleanup owner.
            </remarks>
            <returns>True if the extension was present and contained the key.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.TryGetMinPinLength(System.Int32@)">
            <summary>
            Attempts to get the minPinLength extension output.
            </summary>
            <param name="minLength">The reported minimum in Unicode code points; zero on false is only an out-parameter default.</param>
            <returns>True if the extension was present.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.TryGetRawExtension(System.String,System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte}@)">
            <summary>
            Attempts to get raw extension data by identifier.
            </summary>
            <param name="extensionId">The extension identifier.</param>
            <param name="data">Reconstructed CBOR, or empty data from the identifiers-only reader overload; not an original encoded slice.</param>
            <returns>True if the extension was present.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.Decode(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Reconstructs supported extension values from CBOR bytes into independent encoded copies.
            </summary>
            <param name="data">The CBOR-encoded extensions map.</param>
            <returns>The convenience output, subject to the reconstruction and ownership limits in the class remarks.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.Decode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Decodes extension output from a CBOR reader.
            </summary>
            <param name="reader">The CBOR reader positioned at the extensions map.</param>
            <returns>The decoded extension output.</returns>
            <remarks>
            This overload retains identifiers only and stores empty data after skipping each value.
            HasExtensions/ExtensionIds remain usable, but typed value accessors are not usable on its output.
            Use the memory overload for limited value reconstruction, or retain source raw bytes for exact data.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Extensions.ExtensionOutput.DecodeWithRawData(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Reconstructs supported extension values from CBOR bytes; the name does not imply byte-exact preservation.
            </summary>
            <param name="data">The CBOR-encoded extensions map.</param>
            <returns>Independent reconstructed values with the class-level unknown-data/cleanup limitations.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session">
            <summary>
            Interface for CTAP2 session operations on a YubiKey authenticator.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Exposes CTAP2 operations and selected optional features. Availability depends on the
            authenticator's advertised capabilities, current configuration, product, firmware and transport;
            advertisement alone does not grant PIN/UV permissions or establish support for every operation.
            CTAP2.1 reference: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html
            </para>
            <para>
            Await each call before starting another exchange. The session refuses overlapping exchanges,
            rather than queuing them, and does not reserve the authenticator across a multi-command sequence.
            A pre-canceled exchange is refused before wire admission.
            Cancellation is cooperative: admitted SmartCard exchanges complete, while HID cancellation is
            observed during keep-alive processing and the terminal response is drained. Cancellation can race
            a successful return and does not impose a host deadline or undo device work. A transport,
            notification callback or decoder failure is not proof that the authenticator made no change.
            </para>
            <para>
            User-presence notifications describe SDK policy or an observed HID wait. Their completion reflects
            the CTAP exchange before typed decoding, not verified UP/UV flags or relying-party authentication.
            The relying party remains responsible for challenge, origin, account binding, signature,
            attestation and requested UP/UV verification, including its counter policy.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.SendCborRequestAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Sends a raw CTAP CBOR request to the authenticator.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This is a low-level method for advanced scenarios. Most users should use the
            higher-level methods like <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.MakeCredentialAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialRpEntity,Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity,System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList{Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.PublicKeyCredentialParameters},Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)"/> and <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.GetAssertionAsync(System.String,System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)"/>.
            </para>
            <para>
            The request must include the CTAP command byte as the first byte, followed by
            the CBOR-encoded parameters (if any). The caller selects the command schema, authorization
            and stateful sequence, and must meet CTAP canonical encoding, nesting and device message-size
            limits. This method does not perform capability, PIN/UV or command-schema preflight and does
            not infer user-presence notifications. Transport framing and CTAP status handling still apply.
            CTAP2.1 §8 limits nesting to four levels and messages to 1024 bytes unless GetInfo maxMsgSize
            advertises a larger limit; the session does not enforce that device limit at this boundary.
            </para>
            <para>
            Keep request storage valid and unchanged until the call completes, and clear caller-owned
            secrets when no longer needed. The returned read-only view has no disposable or automatic
            zeroing contract; clearing a copy does not clear the backend's response storage.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <param name="request">The serialized CTAP request (command byte + CBOR payload).</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>The successful response payload without the CTAP status byte; it can be empty.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The request has no command byte.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">A nonzero CTAP status is received, or Other is synthesized
            for a response with no status byte. Transport/APDU errors have separate origins.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.GetInfoAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Queries the authenticator for information at the time of this call.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Each call sends GetInfo; options may change after PIN or configuration operations.
            This read does not refresh the session's construction-time firmware or protocol configuration.
            Do not insert GetInfo into a stateful assertion or administrative continuation sequence.
            </remarks>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>The authenticator information.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.SelectionAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Requests user presence to select this authenticator.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            This command is useful when multiple authenticators are present and the user
            needs to indicate which one they want to use. Presence depends on the transport and device.
            The caller coordinates other authenticators and cancels their outstanding selection requests.
            HID can report a device-wait notification; SmartCard does not predict a touch notification here.
            </remarks>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.ResetAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Resets the FIDO application to factory defaults.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Reset invalidates generated credentials, including non-discoverable and CTAP1/U2F credentials,
            erases discoverable credentials and clears the FIDO PIN. Storage and configuration reset
            effects depend on the applicable protocol revision and product; this is not a device-wide reset.
            YubiKey Bio Multi-protocol Edition requires device-wide reset instead when individual FIDO reset
            is blocked; this method does not choose or perform that alternate product procedure.
            </para>
            <para>
            Send reset promptly after power-up. CTAP2.1 and CTAP2.3 §6.6 specify command receipt within
            ten seconds for displayless authenticators, separately from the subsequent presence wait.
            Yubico documents ten seconds for firmware 5.5.4 and later and five seconds before 5.5.2;
            that product guidance does not classify 5.5.2/5.5.3. Its USB touch wait is separately thirty
            seconds. Meet the product's transport and any enabled long-touch requirements; inspect
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.AuthenticatorInfo.TransportsForReset"/> and <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.AuthenticatorInfo.LongTouchForReset"/>
            where advertised. The authenticator enforces these conditions; this method does not arrange
            power cycling, enforce a local clock, refresh session state or roll back an attempted reset.
            Reset is destructive and cannot be undone.
            </para>
            <para>
            Product procedure: https://docs.yubico.com/yesdk/users-manual/application-fido2/fido2-reset.html
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">
            Thrown with <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapStatus.NotAllowed"/> if reset is attempted too long after
            power-up; other reset refusals and presence timeouts can have different CTAP statuses.
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.MakeCredentialAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialRpEntity,Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.PublicKeyCredentialUserEntity,System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList{Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.PublicKeyCredentialParameters},Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Creates a new credential on the authenticator.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This method implements the CTAP2 authenticatorMakeCredential command.
            User presence is requested; <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.UserPresence"/> cannot be false.
            The device's presence gesture depends on transport and policy, not always a physical touch.
            </para>
            <para>
            For discoverable credentials, set <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.MakeCredentialOptions.ResidentKey"/> to true.
            The caller constructs serialized client data and supplies its SHA-256 hash, not the raw RP
            challenge. The session checks the hash length, not its contents or the RP ID's origin authority.
            Preserve credential ID and user/account mapping and have the relying party verify the response.
            </para>
            <para>
            Built-in UV is requested with UserVerification only on a capable authenticator. When supplying
            PinUvAuthParam, omit UserVerification entirely (including false), use the appropriate protocol
            and authenticate this exact hash with a token authorized for MakeCredential and this RP.
            Legacy PIN-token fallback does not request explicit permissions/RP scope; select that route
            only when the authenticator's applicable legacy authorization rules permit the operation.
            The encoder does not negotiate capabilities or reject every invalid UV/token combination.
            Keep borrowed entity IDs, option buffers and collections stable through completion. The session
            clears its encoded request in finally, not caller inputs or decoded secret-bearing responses;
            session disposal is not sensitive-result cleanup. CTAP success precedes decoding and is not
            complete WebAuthn registration verification.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <param name="clientDataHash">The 32-byte SHA-256 hash of serialized client data.</param>
            <param name="rp">Relying party entity.</param>
            <param name="user">User entity.</param>
            <param name="pubKeyCredParams">Supported credential parameters in preference order.</param>
            <param name="options">Optional parameters including exclude list, extensions, etc.</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>The created credential response with attestation.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The hash is not 32 bytes, UserPresence is false,
            or the credential parameter list is empty or contains duplicate type/algorithm pairs.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">
            Thrown with <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapStatus.CredentialExcluded"/> when the authenticator's applicable
            RP, credential and authorization processing finds an excluded credential, not a global duplicate-user check.
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.GetAssertionAsync(System.String,System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Gets an assertion for authentication.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This method implements the CTAP2 authenticatorGetAssertion command.
            User presence defaults to requested. Setting <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionOptions.UserPresence"/>
            to false sends a silent request and suppresses the SDK notification, subject to device policy;
            neither a notification nor its absence verifies the returned UP/UV flags.
            </para>
            <para>
            If multiple credentials match, use <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.GetNextAssertionAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)"/> to retrieve
            additional assertions according to the returned count. The caller supplies the SHA-256 hash
            of serialized client data, retains credential/account associations and has the relying party
            verify the proof. This method does not construct client data, authorize the RP ID against an
            origin or verify signatures. When supplying PinUvAuthParam, omit UserVerification entirely
            and use the matching protocol and GetAssertion permission/RP scope for the exact hash.
            Legacy token fallback has no explicit permission/RP request; applicable device authorization
            rules still govern its use. With no allow list, the request asks for applicable discoverable
            credentials for this RP, not a global credential or account search.
            </para>
            <para>
            Keep borrowed option buffers and collections stable through completion. Only the session's
            encoded request is cleared in finally; caller inputs and decoded response copies are not
            cleared by this method or session disposal. Callback or decode failure after CTAP success
            does not imply the device did nothing.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <param name="rpId">Relying party identifier.</param>
            <param name="clientDataHash">The 32-byte SHA-256 hash of serialized client data.</param>
            <param name="options">Optional parameters including allow list, extensions, etc.</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>The first assertion response.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The RP ID is null/empty or the hash is not 32 bytes.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">
            Thrown with <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapStatus.NoCredentials"/> if no matching credential is found.
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session.GetNextAssertionAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Gets the next assertion when multiple credentials match.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Call this method when <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Credentials.GetAssertionResponse.NumberOfCredentials"/> is greater than 1.
            Collect N−1 additional responses promptly after the first count N. An absent count means one
            at the protocol level. Do not interpose GetInfo, PIN, administrative, raw or other authenticator
            operations, including on another channel. This method sends no new presence or PIN request
            and tracks no local remaining count, timer or sequence reservation. CTAP2.1 §6.3 allows
            NotAllowed for missing, exhausted or expired state (more than thirty seconds between calls);
            its timeout step is optional over NFC. An exchange guard is not a lease for the whole sequence.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>The next assertion response.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions">
            <summary>
            Extension methods for creating CTAP2 sessions from YubiKey devices.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            These extension methods provide a convenient API for working with CTAP2
            functionality on YubiKey devices. They automatically handle connection management
            and session creation.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions.GetCtap2InfoAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Abstractions.IYubiKey,Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Sessions.SessionCreationOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <inheritdoc cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions.&lt;G&gt;$530A81414B90DCDCE8D59F69B4A6A77B.GetCtap2InfoAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Sessions.SessionCreationOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)"/>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions.CreateCtap2SessionAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Abstractions.IYubiKey,Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Sessions.SessionCreationOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <inheritdoc cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions.&lt;G&gt;$530A81414B90DCDCE8D59F69B4A6A77B.CreateCtap2SessionAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Sessions.SessionCreationOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)"/>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions.ResolveCtap2SessionTransport(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Abstractions.IYubiKey,System.Nullable{Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionType})">
            <inheritdoc cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions.&lt;G&gt;$530A81414B90DCDCE8D59F69B4A6A77B.ResolveCtap2SessionTransport(System.Nullable{Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionType})"/>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions.&lt;G&gt;$530A81414B90DCDCE8D59F69B4A6A77B.GetCtap2InfoAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Sessions.SessionCreationOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Gets CTAP2 authenticator information from a YubiKey asynchronously.
            </summary>
            <param name="options">Optional cross-cutting session creation settings.</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">An optional token to cancel the operation.</param>
            <returns>
            An <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.AuthenticatorInfo"/> containing detailed information about the 
            authenticator's capabilities, supported extensions, and options.
            </returns>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This is a convenience method that creates a temporary CTAP2 session, retrieves
            the authenticator info, and disposes of the session and its owned connection. Creation
            performs an initial GetInfo probe; this method then sends a second, fresh GetInfo read.
            It needs no PIN or presence for GetInfo itself. For multiple operations,
            use <c>CreateCtap2SessionAsync</c> instead to reuse the session.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <example>
            Composable fragment with an available <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Abstractions.IYubiKey"/> named yubiKey; reported
            version advertisement is not certification or support for every optional feature.
            <code>
            var info = await yubiKey.GetCtap2InfoAsync();
            Console.WriteLine($"AAGUID: {Convert.ToHexString(info.Aaguid.Span)}");
            Console.WriteLine($"Supports CTAP2.1: {info.Versions.Contains("FIDO_2_1")}");
            </code>
            </example>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions.&lt;G&gt;$530A81414B90DCDCE8D59F69B4A6A77B.CreateCtap2SessionAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Sessions.SessionCreationOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Creates a CTAP2 session for interacting with a YubiKey asynchronously.
            </summary>
            <param name="options">
            Optional creation settings. CTAP2 selects HID FIDO, then SmartCard unless
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Sessions.SessionCreationOptions.PreferredConnectionType" /> specifies a supported transport.
            Secure-channel parameters force SmartCard when no preference is specified.
            </param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">An optional token to cancel the operation.</param>
            <returns>
            A <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Ctap2Session"/> instance configured for the YubiKey device.
            The session must be disposed by the caller when no longer needed.
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.NotSupportedException">
            Thrown if the YubiKey does not expose a FIDO-capable connection
            (<see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionType.HidFido"/> or <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionType.SmartCard"/>), or if an
            explicitly preferred connection is valid for CTAP2 but not exposed by this device.
            </exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">
            Thrown if the preferred connection is not a single concrete transport or is a
            transport CTAP2 cannot use (for example <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionType.HidOtp"/>).
            </exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionInUseException">The physical YubiKey already has a live connection.</exception>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            CTAP2 sessions can be created over two transport types:
            <list type="bullet">
            <item><description>FIDO HID: Uses CTAP HID protocol for USB communication (the default first choice)</description></item>
            <item><description>SmartCard (CCID): Uses ISO 7816-4 APDUs over the FIDO AID (NFC, or USB on firmware 5.8.0+)</description></item>
            </list>
            When a device exposes both, the default selects HID FIDO. Set
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Sessions.SessionCreationOptions.PreferredConnectionType" /> to
            <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionType.SmartCard"/> to force SmartCard.
            </para>
            <para>
            SCP (Secure Channel Protocol) is supported only on SmartCard. Supplying
            secure-channel parameters without an explicit preference selects SmartCard automatically.
            Explicitly selecting HID FIDO with SCP parameters causes session initialization to throw
            <see cref="T:System.NotSupportedException"/> before HID channel initialization or GetInfo.
            </para>
            <para>
            The returned session owns the opened connection; dispose it before opening another session
            on the same physical YubiKey. Connection failures do not trigger another transport attempt.
            Caller-supplied SCP parameters and UserPresencePrompt remain caller-owned. SmartCard
            selection and GetInfo precede the detected-firmware USB gate and SCP establishment;
            FirmwareVersionOverride changes configured session firmware, not that gate's detected value.
            Major == 0 sentinel/missing firmware passes Feature's optimistic check, not a hardware
            firmware qualification. SCP authentication does not grant CTAP PIN/UV token permissions.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <example>
            Two alternative composable fragments with an available <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Abstractions.IYubiKey"/> named yubiKey.
            The SCP03 alternative requires an authorized SmartCard device provisioned with the supplied
            default keys; the defaults are not a production key-management recommendation.
            <code>
            // Ordinary session: dispose before opening another connection on this physical key.
            {
                await using var session = await yubiKey.CreateCtap2SessionAsync();
                var info = await session.GetInfoAsync();
            }
            
            // Alternative: SCP03 over SmartCard on a device provisioned for these keys.
            using var scpKeys = Scp03KeyParameters.Default;
            await using var secureSession = await yubiKey.CreateCtap2SessionAsync(
                new SessionCreationOptions
                {
                    ScpKeyParameters = scpKeys,
                    PreferredConnectionType = ConnectionType.SmartCard
                });
            </code>
            </example>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IYubiKeyExtensions.&lt;G&gt;$530A81414B90DCDCE8D59F69B4A6A77B.ResolveCtap2SessionTransport(System.Nullable{Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionType})">
            <summary>
            Resolves the single transport selected for CTAP2.
            </summary>
            <param name="preferredConnection">Optional explicit transport override (see CreateCtap2SessionAsync).</param>
            <returns>The selected CTAP2 transport.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.ILargeBlobStorage">
            <summary>
            Per-credential large-blob storage over authenticatorLargeBlobs (CTAP 2.1-2.3 §6.10). Implemented by
            <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage"/>; an interface so clients built on it can be tested without a device.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            LargeBlobStorage uses the largeBlobKey response-envelope route, not direct largeBlob extension
            outputs. It borrows its session/protocol/token and caches GetInfo limits per instance. Callers must
            coordinate whole multi-command operations on the shared array/session; no transaction, conflict
            detection, rollback or resume is provided. Cancellation/failure can follow device changes.
            Actual writes require protocol/token configuration in this SDK even where CTAP permits an
            unverified write. Keep borrowed key/data storage stable through each await; clear caller-owned
            secrets and returned plaintext afterward. SDK internal copies are not comprehensively cleared.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.ILargeBlobStorage.ReadLargeBlobArrayAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Reads the whole array; a short or corrupt array is the initial (empty) array (§6.10.2).</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.ILargeBlobStorage.WriteLargeBlobArrayAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Replaces the whole shared array; this SDK requires a protocol/token with LargeBlobWrite.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.ILargeBlobStorage.GetBlobAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Returns caller-owned plaintext to clear after use, or null when no entry decrypts within the SDK read cap.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.ILargeBlobStorage.SetBlobAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Reads, modifies and rewrites the full array to replace matching decryptable entries (§6.10.5).</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.ILargeBlobStorage.DeleteBlobAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Rewrites the array without matching decryptable entries; false when none matched within the read cap.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry">
            <summary>
            One element of the CTAP large-blob array (CTAP 2.1-2.3 §6.10.3 "large-blob map structure"):
            <c>{1: ciphertext, 2: nonce, 3: origSize}</c>.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Writing (§6.10.5): the data is compressed with raw DEFLATE (RFC 1951), then encrypted with
            AEAD_AES_256_GCM under the credential's largeBlobKey with a fresh 12-byte nonce and the associated
            data <c>"blob" || uint64LittleEndian(origSize)</c>; the 16-byte tag is appended to the ciphertext.
            </para>
            <para>
            Reading (§6.10.4): an entry that does not decrypt under the key is simply not this credential's
            ("skip this array element"); a decrypted entry whose inflation fails or whose inflated length is
            not origSize is an error. This SDK skips origSize above 1 MiB before decryption: a platform limit
            chosen from the §6.10.4 SHOULD note, not a universal protocol maximum. Encrypt has no matching cap.
            </para>
            <para>
            Unknown elements of accepted maps retain their encoded key/value bytes (§6.10.3 permits unknown
            elements), while known fields and the enclosing maps are reconstructed. This is not byte-exact
            preservation of a foreign entry or the complete array. Nonconforming entries are skipped; origSize
            and integer map keys are limited to the signed Int64 range. Unknown values retain encoded slices,
            including unsigned values beyond Int64, subject to reader/writer conformance requirements.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.MaxOriginalSize">
            <summary>
            The largest origSize this SDK will inflate: 1 MiB, the minimum CTAP §6.10.4 asks platforms to
            permit ("that maximum SHOULD be at least 1MiB").
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.#ctor(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Int64)">
            <summary>Creates an entry by borrowing ciphertext and nonce storage without copying it.</summary>
            <param name="ciphertext">AEAD_AES_256_GCM ciphertext with the 16-byte tag at the end.</param>
            <param name="nonce">The 12-byte AEAD nonce.</param>
            <param name="originalSize">The length of the uncompressed data.</param>
            <remarks>Keep borrowed storage unchanged while this entry is used or serialized. Read-only views are not immutable storage.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.Ciphertext">
            <summary>§6.10.3 element 1: the AEAD ciphertext, "implicitly including the AEAD authentication tag at the end".</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.Nonce">
            <summary>§6.10.3 element 2: the AEAD nonce, "MUST be exactly 12 bytes long".</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.OriginalSize">
            <summary>§6.10.3 element 3: "the length, in bytes, of the uncompressed data".</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.TryDecrypt(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Attempts to decrypt this entry with a credential's largeBlobKey.
            </summary>
            <param name="largeBlobKey">The 32-byte largeBlobKey.</param>
            <returns>Caller-owned plaintext to clear after use, or null for authentication failure or origSize above the SDK read cap.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.IO.InvalidDataException">
            The entry decrypted under this key but its content is not valid: inflation failed or the inflated
            length differs from <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.OriginalSize"/> (CTAP §6.10.4: "return an error").
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.TryDecrypt(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.Action{System.Byte[]})">
            <summary>Test seam: observes the allocated compressed plaintext and, if reached, inflation buffer after clearing; not every SDK/provider copy.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.Encrypt(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Creates an entry for <paramref name="data"/> under a credential's largeBlobKey (CTAP §6.10.5).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Borrows key/data for this call and returns new ciphertext/nonce arrays. Clear caller-owned
            plaintext/key storage after use. The returned compressed array is cleared, but this does not
            clear the compression stream's backing storage or establish end-to-end provider cleanup.
            Data above MaxOriginalSize is accepted here but cannot be returned by TryDecrypt.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.Encode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborWriter)">
            <summary>Encodes the §6.10.3 map (canonical CBOR), unknown elements included.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.TryDecode(System.Formats.Cbor.CborReader)">
            <summary>
            Decodes one array element. Returns null when the element is not a conforming map (§6.10.4: "skip
            this array element"); the reader is left after the element either way.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.AssociatedData(System.Int64)">
            <summary>§6.10.3: "The value 0x626c6f62 ("blob") || uint64LittleEndian(origSize)".</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.Deflate(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>§6.10.5: "Let plaintext equal origData after compression with DEFLATE [RFC1951]" (raw, no zlib header).</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry.Inflate(System.Byte[],System.Int64,System.Action{System.Byte[]})">
            <summary>
            §6.10.4: inflate, "If decompression fails, return an error. If the length of the decompression result
            is not equal to origSize, return an error." Reads at most origSize + 1 bytes so an inflation bomb
            cannot exceed the cap.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray">
            <summary>
            The large-blob array stored on the authenticator (CTAP 2.1-2.3 §6.10.2): a canonical CBOR array of
            <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry"/> maps followed by the first 16 bytes of SHA-256 over the array.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Entries supplied through init are borrowed as a list, not snapshotted. Keep list and entry storage
            stable during use. Deserialization retains only accepted modeled entries, not a complete raw array;
            rewrites may discard nonconforming entries and reconstruct known fields. No universal foreign-client
            interoperability or byte-exact preservation guarantee follows from this representation.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray.Entries">
            <summary>The conforming entries, in array order.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray.Deserialize(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Deserializes a large-blob array, verifying the trailing hash. Elements that are not conforming
            large-blob maps are skipped (§6.10.4).
            </summary>
            <param name="data">Serialized array storage; keep it alive and unchanged while retained unknown elements may be used or serialized.</param>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The data is too short or the hash does not match.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.Formats.Cbor.CborContentException">CBOR is malformed or violates the reader's conformance requirements.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException">A typed read encounters the wrong CBOR major type, including a non-array root.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.OverflowException">An origSize or integer map key is outside the signed Int64 range.</exception>
            <remarks>
            Known ciphertext/nonce byte strings are independently copied, but retained unknown encoded
            keys/values borrow slices of data. The result is therefore not a fully detached snapshot.
            Rejects short/hash-corrupt input for direct callers; this does not validate every complete-envelope
            or unsigned-range condition. <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.ReadLargeBlobArrayAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)"/> applies
            §6.10.2's rule that a short or corrupt array is treated as the initial (empty) array.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray.HasValidHash(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>§6.10.2: the trailing 16 bytes are LEFT(SHA-256(array), 16); anything else is "the initial large-blob array".</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray.Serialize">
            <summary>Serializes the array with its trailing hash (canonical CBOR, §6.10.2).</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray.CreateEmpty">
            <summary>The initial large-blob array: no entries.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray.WithEntry(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobEntry)">
            <summary>Returns a new array with <paramref name="entry"/> appended.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray.WithoutEntry(System.Int32)">
            <summary>Returns a new array without the entry at <paramref name="index"/>.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray.FindAndDecrypt(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>Returns caller-owned plaintext from the first entry that decrypts within the SDK read cap, or null; clear returned plaintext after use.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage">
            <summary>
            Provides operations for reading and writing large blobs on FIDO2 authenticators.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The authenticatorLargeBlobs command allows storing arbitrary data associated with
            discoverable credentials. Data is encrypted using the credential's largeBlobKey,
            returned in the credential response envelope when largeBlobKey is requested. Do not assume the
            authenticator derives this random storage key from the credential private key. Check both
            largeBlobKey advertisement and largeBlobs:true; this helper does not perform capability preflight.
            </para>
            <para>
            Large blobs share one serialized array. Reading ciphertext needs no PIN/UV parameter here, but
            returning a credential's plaintext requires its key. Actual writes always require a supplied
            protocol/token in this SDK, stricter than CTAP 2.3 §6.10.2's conditional device UV rule.
            The device checks the opaque token's authorization when configured UV or alwaysUv:true requires it;
            this helper does not inspect token permissions, validity or expiry.
            </para>
            <para>
            For credentials created with largeBlobKey, use
            <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.GetBlobAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)"/> and
            <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.SetBlobAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)"/>
            to read/write blobs for specific credentials.
            The alternative direct largeBlob extension is not implemented by this helper.
            </para>
            <para>
            Limits are cached per helper from GetInfo: fragment length is maxMsgSize minus 64 (default 960),
            and the reported maximum serialized array size gates writes. Normally these limits remain cached;
            a write with no cached maximum array size reloads GetInfo and refreshes the fragment limit too.
            Reads continue until a short/empty fragment; writes send sequential chunks with total length only
            on the first chunk and authentication on each. Intermediate success is not a complete-array commit.
            Coordinate the entire operation with other users of the session/shared array: there is no
            sequence-wide lock, conflict detection, rollback or resume. After failure/cancellation, re-read
            state rather than assuming no write occurred or blindly resuming at the failed offset.
            </para>
            <para>
            The session, protocol and token are borrowed, not disposed or cleared by this helper. Keep them
            usable and token storage unchanged throughout each awaited operation. Returned plaintext arrays
            are caller-owned; clear them and caller-owned keys/data when finished, including later failures.
            Internal membership probes, compression and authenticated-request copies are not comprehensively
            cleared, so this is not an end-to-end sensitive-data cleanup guarantee.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.#ctor(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session)">
            <summary>Creates read-only storage. Fragment sizes come from the authenticator's GetInfo.</summary>
            <param name="session">A borrowed initialized session; keep it open through each operation.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.#ctor(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session,Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol,System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte})">
            <summary>Creates read/write storage; writes need a PIN/UV token with the LargeBlobWrite permission.</summary>
            <param name="session">A borrowed initialized session.</param>
            <param name="protocol">A borrowed usable protocol matching the token; this helper does not dispose it.</param>
            <param name="pinUvAuthToken">Borrowed token with LargeBlobWrite authorization; keep storage stable until operations finish, then clear it when no longer needed.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.GetMaxFragmentLengthAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            CTAP §6.10.2: "maxFragmentLength = maxMsgSize − 64" with GetInfo's maxMsgSize (default 1024, §6.4).
            Cached per instance; LoadLimitsAsync can refresh it when a write has no reported maximum array size.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.ReadLargeBlobArrayAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Reads the entire large blob array from the authenticator.
            </summary>
            <param name="cancellationToken">The cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>The large blob array.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Short/hash-corrupt data becomes the initial empty array. The current response parser also treats
            missing config or an empty successful response as an empty fragment; this is a decoding limitation,
            not evidence of a conforming empty device array. Malformed CBOR behind a valid hash can throw.
            </remarks>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">Thrown when the operation fails.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.WriteLargeBlobArrayAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobArray,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Writes the entire large blob array to the authenticator.
            </summary>
            <param name="array">The array to write.</param>
            <remarks>
            Replaces the complete shared array, not only one credential's entry. Keep entry/list storage
            unchanged until completion and preserve other clients' entries where possible. A failed call
            can leave changed/torn state; there is no transactional rollback or conflict detection.
            </remarks>
            <param name="cancellationToken">The cancellation token.</param>
            <exception cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException">Thrown when PIN/UV auth is not configured.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">Thrown when the operation fails.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.GetBlobAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Gets the blob data for a specific credential.
            </summary>
            <param name="largeBlobKey">The credential's largeBlobKey (32 bytes).</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">The cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>Caller-owned plaintext to clear after use, or null if no entry decrypts within the SDK's 1 MiB read cap.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">Thrown when largeBlobKey is not 32 bytes.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">Thrown when reading fails.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.IO.InvalidDataException">A decrypted entry cannot inflate to its declared original size.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.SetBlobAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Sets the blob data for a specific credential.
            </summary>
            <param name="largeBlobKey">The credential's largeBlobKey (32 bytes).</param>
            <param name="data">The data to store.</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">The cancellation token.</param>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This operation replaces entries that decrypt with this key within the SDK read cap.
            It reads the current array, removes those matching entries,
            adds the new encrypted entry, and writes the array back.
            This is a full-array read-modify-write, not an atomic per-credential update. Foreign entries are
            preserved only within LargeBlobArray's modeled scope. No 1 MiB plaintext write cap is enforced,
            although larger entries cannot be returned by this SDK's read helper. Inputs are borrowed through
            the completed await. Successful membership probes currently leave discarded plaintext copies.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">Thrown when largeBlobKey is not 32 bytes.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException">Thrown when PIN/UV auth is not configured.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">Thrown when the operation fails.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.DeleteBlobAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Deletes the blob data for a specific credential.
            </summary>
            <param name="largeBlobKey">The credential's largeBlobKey (32 bytes).</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">The cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>True after rewriting the array without matching decryptable entries; false when none matched, including entries above the read cap.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Reads and rewrites the full shared array without a transaction or conflict lock. A read-only
            helper can return false without writing; a matching entry requires configured write authentication.
            Successful membership probes currently leave discarded plaintext copies. Failure/cancellation
            does not establish rollback; re-read storage before deciding how to recover.
            </remarks>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">Thrown when largeBlobKey is not 32 bytes.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.InvalidOperationException">Thrown when PIN/UV auth is not configured.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">Thrown when the operation fails.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.ReadRawBlobAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Reads raw blob data from the authenticator (for advanced use).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.ReadFragmentAsync(System.Int32,System.Int32,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Reads a single fragment from the blob.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.WriteRawBlobAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Writes raw blob data to the authenticator (for advanced use).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.LargeBlobs.LargeBlobStorage.WriteFragmentAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Int32,System.Int32,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Writes a single fragment to the blob.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin">
            <summary>
            Provides PIN and UV token management operations for CTAP2 authenticators.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            ClientPin handles the CTAP2 authenticatorClientPin command, which manages:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>Setting and changing PINs</description></item>
              <item><description>Getting PIN and UV retry counts</description></item>
              <item><description>Obtaining PIN/UV auth tokens for credential operations</description></item>
            </list>
            </para>
            <para>
            Select a mutually supported protocol from authenticatorGetInfo's PinUvAuthProtocols before
            constructing this helper. The helper does not negotiate V1/V2. It borrows the session but owns
            disposal of the supplied protocol; keep the session open until all helper operations complete.
            Each PIN set/change or token request performs fresh key agreement.
            </para>
            <para>
            Supply PINs as NFC-normalized UTF-8, with at least four Unicode characters and no final 0x00
            byte. For a new PIN, also meet the authenticator's current minimum in Unicode code points and
            any additional device policy. The SDK checks only 4–63 input bytes: it does not validate UTF-8,
            normalization, code-point count, a final zero byte or the advertised minimum. It hashes the
            exact supplied bytes, so do not append padding to a PIN argument.
            </para>
            <para>
            If GetInfo reports forcePINChange=true, change the PIN before requesting a PIN token.
            Under original CTAP 2.1, after verifying the correct PIN, legacy getPinToken (0x05) returns
            PIN_INVALID for forced change, while getPinUvAuthTokenUsingPinWithPermissions (0x09) returns
            PIN_POLICY_VIOLATION. PIN_INVALID alone proves neither an incorrect PIN nor forced-change state.
            This helper does not preflight forcePINChange or automatically retry PIN requests.
            </para>
            <para>
            PIN arguments remain caller-owned. Keep them unchanged until the returned task completes,
            faults or is canceled, then clear them when no longer needed. Returned tokens are separate
            caller-owned secrets; clear them after their last use. The helper clears its named shared-secret,
            PIN-hash and padded-PIN buffers in finally blocks, not every builder/request/response copy.
            Disposal does not provide end-to-end secret erasure or invalidate tokens on the authenticator.
            </para>
            <para>
            The authenticator enforces token scope and lifetime. Ordinary tokens can expire, lose permissions
            after user-presence checks, or be invalidated by another token issuance, PIN change, power cycle
            or reset. A host byte array remaining readable is not evidence that its token is still authorized.
            When authorizing MakeCredential or GetAssertion with pinUvAuthParam, omit the uv option key,
            even false. Inspect the returned authenticator data for the operation's verification result.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#authenticatorClientPIN
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.#ctor(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.ICtap2Session,Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol)">
            <summary>
            Initializes a new instance of the <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin"/> class.
            </summary>
            <param name="session">The borrowed CTAP2 session. This helper does not dispose it.</param>
            <param name="protocol">The caller-selected, mutually supported protocol. Disposing this helper disposes this supplied object; do not share it with a longer-lived consumer.</param>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentNullException">If session or protocol is null.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.Protocol">
            <summary>
            Gets the PIN/UV auth protocol used by this instance.
            </summary>
            <remarks>This property remains readable after disposal and returns the same, then-disposed protocol reference. It does not extend that protocol's usable lifetime.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.GetPinRetriesAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Reads a snapshot of the PIN retry count and optional power-cycle state.
            </summary>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>The authenticator's current PIN retry status.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Missing response fields currently default to zero retries and false power-cycle state;
            false therefore does not prove another attempt is safe. PIN_AUTH_BLOCKED indicates a
            temporary block requiring a power cycle, whereas PIN_BLOCKED indicates exhausted retries
            requiring reset. Do not blindly retry an incorrect PIN.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.GetUvRetriesAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Reads a snapshot of the built-in user-verification retry count (CTAP 2.1).
            </summary>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>The authenticator's current user-verification retry status.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Missing counts currently default to zero. CTAP 2.1 defines no power-cycle field for this
            response; the result's false default is not recovery evidence. Exhausted built-in UV retries
            can be re-enabled by reset or a successful configured ClientPIN token request. This method
            does not attempt recovery or decide whether the caller should fall back to PIN.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.SetPinAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Sets a new PIN on the authenticator (first-time setup).
            </summary>
            <param name="newPin">
                The borrowed, unpadded NFC UTF-8 new PIN, 4–63 bytes. Meet the current device minimum
                in code points and additional policy; the SDK checks byte length only. Keep the buffer
                unchanged through task completion and clear it after its last use, including on failure.
            </param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If the PIN byte length is invalid.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">If the authenticator rejects setup, for example because a PIN is already set or device PIN policy is not met.</exception>
            <remarks>The PIN must not end in 0x00. This method right-zero-pads it to exactly 64 bytes before encryption; AES adds no padding.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.ChangePinAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Changes the existing PIN on the authenticator.
            </summary>
            <param name="currentPin">
                The borrowed, unpadded NFC UTF-8 current PIN, 4–63 bytes, with no final 0x00.
                Keep it unchanged through task completion and clear it after its last use, including on failure.
            </param>
            <param name="newPin">
                The borrowed, unpadded NFC UTF-8 new PIN, 4–63 bytes, with no final 0x00. Meet the
                current device minimum in code points and additional policy; the SDK checks byte length
                only. Keep it unchanged through task completion and clear it after its last use.
            </param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If either PIN byte length is invalid.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">If the authenticator rejects the change, including an incorrect/blocked current PIN or a new PIN that violates policy.</exception>
            <remarks>
            A successful change invalidates existing authenticator tokens. This helper does not retain
            authorization state or roll the change back; a failed or canceled call is not proof that
            the device PIN remained unchanged.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.GetPinTokenAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Requests a token with the legacy getPinToken subcommand using the PIN.
            </summary>
            <param name="pin">
                The borrowed, unpadded NFC UTF-8 PIN, 4–63 bytes, with no final 0x00. The SDK checks
                byte length only. Keep it unchanged through task completion and clear it after its last use.
            </param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>A new caller-owned decrypted token. Clear it after its last use, including if a subsequent operation fails. CTAP V1 tokens are 16 or 32 bytes; V2 tokens are 32 bytes. This helper does not validate the decrypted token length.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If the PIN byte length is outside 4–63 bytes.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">If the PIN is incorrect.</exception>
            <remarks>
            Use <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol.Authenticate(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})"/> to compute pinUvAuthParam, not to
            establish device authorization. Under CTAP 2.1, legacy tokens receive default MakeCredential
            and GetAssertion permissions and bind to the RP on first use, unless
            noMcGaPermissionsWithClientPin suppresses those permissions. This command sends no explicit
            permissions or RP ID; it does not grant arbitrary administrative permissions. PIN token
            issuance does not itself establish user presence.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.GetPinUvAuthTokenUsingPinAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions,System.String,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Requests a PIN/UV auth token using PIN, with explicit permissions when supported.
            </summary>
            <param name="pin">
                The borrowed, unpadded NFC UTF-8 PIN, 4–63 bytes, with no final 0x00. The SDK checks
                byte length only. Keep it unchanged through task completion and clear it after its last use.
            </param>
            <param name="permissions">The nonzero permissions to request. The caller must choose a valid combination supported by the authenticator; only None is locally rejected.</param>
            <param name="rpId">Required for MakeCredential/GetAssertion permissions; optional to restrict CredentialManagement to one RP; ignored for BioEnrollment, LargeBlobWrite, AuthenticatorConfig and CredentialManagementRO. Null or empty omits the field.</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>A new caller-owned decrypted token. Clear it after its last use, including on subsequent failure. CTAP V1 tokens are 16 or 32 bytes; V2 tokens are 32 bytes; decrypted length is not checked here. The array carries no permission, RP, expiry or persistence metadata.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If the PIN byte length is outside 4–63 bytes or permissions is None.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">If the PIN is incorrect or permissions are invalid.</exception>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This method calls the supplied session's GetInfoAsync. With a concrete Ctap2Session,
            that is a fresh authenticator query. If and only if options contains pinUvAuthToken=true,
            it sends getPinUvAuthTokenUsingPinWithPermissions (0x09). Otherwise it calls legacy
            getPinToken (0x05), dropping the requested permissions and RP ID. The supplied protocol
            version is unchanged, and a failed 0x09 exchange is not retried with 0x05.
            </para>
            <para>
            Permission-token issuance requires a configured clientPin and pinUvAuthToken=true.
            The authenticator also checks operation capabilities and noMcGaPermissionsWithClientPin;
            this helper does not preflight these checks or enforce RP requirements. PIN acquisition
            does not establish user presence, and no PIN retry loop is performed.
            </para>
            <para>
            CredentialManagementRO is CTAP 2.2's persistent read-only permission (pcmr). Request it
            alone, only with perCredMgmtRO=true; the authenticator ignores RP ID. Ordinary token timers
            are not its lifetime contract. This helper does not check those conditions or model persistent
            token identity; legacy fallback cannot request pcmr.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.GetPinUvAuthTokenUsingUvAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions,System.String,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Requests a permission token using the authenticator's configured built-in user verification.
            </summary>
            <param name="permissions">The nonzero permissions to request. Choose a valid, supported combination; CredentialManagementRO must be requested alone.</param>
            <param name="rpId">Required for MakeCredential/GetAssertion; optional to scope CredentialManagement; ignored for BioEnrollment, LargeBlobWrite, AuthenticatorConfig and CredentialManagementRO. Null or empty omits the field.</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>A new caller-owned decrypted token. Clear it after its last use, including on subsequent failure. CTAP V1 tokens are 16 or 32 bytes; V2 tokens are 32 bytes; decrypted length is not checked here. No scope or persistence metadata accompanies the array.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If permissions is None.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.CtapException">If UV fails or permissions are invalid.</exception>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Use this method when GetInfo reports both uv=true and pinUvAuthToken=true and built-in
            UV, such as biometrics, is configured. CTAP 2.1 requires the authenticator to implement
            this subcommand when both option IDs are true; it does not require the caller to invoke it.
            Operation capabilities also apply; BioEnrollment and AuthenticatorConfig additionally
            require uvBioEnroll and uvAcfg respectively. This helper checks only nonzero permissions;
            it does not query GetInfo or preflight these capabilities, configuration or RP requirements.
            </para>
            <para>
            The authenticator performs the verification interaction and may establish user presence.
            This helper uses generic CBOR exchange, so no operation-specific SDK touch notification is
            guaranteed. It performs one token request without an automatic UV retry or PIN fallback;
            the caller or higher-level client decides recovery from UV errors.
            </para>
            <para>
            CredentialManagementRO requests CTAP 2.2's persistent read-only token only when
            perCredMgmtRO=true and no other permission is requested. RP ID is ignored. The helper
            does not enforce those conditions or manage the persistent token's lifetime.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.GetKeyAgreementAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
            Gets the authenticator's key agreement public key.
            </summary>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token.</param>
            <returns>The COSE public key as a dictionary.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.ValidatePin(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.String)">
            <summary>
                Checks only the PIN argument's byte length, not its Unicode encoding or device policy.
            </summary>
            <param name="pin">The supplied, unpadded PIN bytes.</param>
            <param name="paramName">
                The name of the public parameter <paramref name="pin" /> was supplied through. The
                public surface spells this parameter three different ways — <c>pin</c>,
                <c>currentPin</c> and <c>newPin</c> — so the caller has to name its own, otherwise
                <see cref="P:System.ArgumentException.ParamName" /> would report this helper's local name,
                which matches nothing a caller can filter on.
            </param>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">
                Thrown when the supplied data is shorter than <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.PinMinLength" /> bytes or
                longer than <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.PinMaxLength" /> bytes.
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.ClientPin.Dispose">
            <summary>Disposes the supplied protocol and marks this helper disposed, without disposing the borrowed session.</summary>
            <remarks>Repeated disposal has no effect. Operations reject subsequent use; Protocol remains readable. Caller PINs and returned tokens are not cleared by this method.</remarks>
        </member>
