        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions">
            <summary>
            Permission flags for ordinary CTAP 2.1 tokens and the CTAP 2.2 persistent read-only token.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Permissions control what operations a PIN/UV auth token can authorize.
            Ordinary permissions can be combined using bitwise OR when the authenticator supports the
            requested operations. MakeCredential/GetAssertion require an RP ID; CredentialManagement
            optionally binds to one RP. BioEnrollment, LargeBlobWrite and AuthenticatorConfig ignore RP ID.
            CredentialManagementRO is a separate persistent-token request and cannot be combined.
            The authenticator enforces scope and lifetime; these flags alone do not establish authorization.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#permissions
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions.None">
            <summary>No permissions.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions.MakeCredential">
            <summary>Permission to execute authenticatorMakeCredential.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions.GetAssertion">
            <summary>Permission to execute authenticatorGetAssertion.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions.CredentialManagement">
            <summary>Permission to execute authenticatorCredentialManagement.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions.BioEnrollment">
            <summary>Permission to execute authenticatorBioEnrollment.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions.LargeBlobWrite">
            <summary>Permission to authorize large blob writes; it is not required for all reads.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions.AuthenticatorConfig">
            <summary>Permission to execute authenticatorConfig.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthTokenPermissions.CredentialManagementRO">
            <summary>
            Persistent Credential Management Read Only (pcmr, CTAP 2.2).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Requires perCredMgmtRO=true and must be requested without any other permission.
            RP ID is ignored. The returned persistentPinUvAuthToken authorizes read credential-management
            operations, not deletion or modification; its lifetime is distinct from ordinary tokens.
            </para>
            <para>
            CTAP 2.2 also derives the encIdentifier decryption key from this persistent token.
            That does not establish the key contract for every encrypted metadata field. ClientPin
            returns raw token bytes without validating this capability/combination or tracking persistence.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.2-ps-20250714/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.2-ps-20250714.html#pcmr
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol">
            <summary>
            PIN/UV authentication protocol for CTAP2 authenticators.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The PIN/UV auth protocol provides cryptographic operations for authenticating
            PIN/UV commands and protecting sensitive data in transit.
            </para>
            <para>
            Two protocol versions are defined:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>V1: ECDH P-256, SHA-256(z) (32 bytes), AES-256-CBC with a zero IV, and 16-byte HMAC tags.</description></item>
              <item><description>V2: ECDH P-256, two separate HKDF-SHA-256 derivations (32-byte HMAC key followed by 32-byte AES key), AES-256-CBC with a random IV, and 32-byte HMAC tags.</description></item>
            </list>
            </para>
            <para>
            Inputs are borrowed for the duration of each synchronous call. The caller owns every returned
            byte array and must clear secret-bearing or secret-derived output when no longer needed,
            including on failure in subsequent operations. The V1 and V2 implementations retain no key
            material between calls; disposing them does not clear returned arrays. Their cryptographic
            operations reject use after disposal, but their version and tag-length properties remain readable.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#pinProto
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol.Version">
            <summary>
            Gets the protocol version number (1 or 2).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol.AuthenticationTagLength">
            <summary>
            Gets the length of authentication tags produced by this protocol.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol.Encapsulate(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.Int32,System.Object})">
            <summary>
            Performs ECDH key agreement with the authenticator's public key and derives a shared secret.
            </summary>
            <param name="peerCoseKey">
            The borrowed authenticator key and coordinate arrays, which are neither retained nor cleared.
            CTAP requires kty=2 (EC2), alg=-25, crv=1 (P-256),
            and 32-byte big-endian X and Y coordinates (-2 and -3), with no other optional parameters.
            </param>
            <returns>
            A tuple containing:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>KeyAgreement: A new platform COSE public-key dictionary with exported public coordinates to send to the authenticator. These coordinates are not secret material.</description></item>
              <item><description>SharedSecret: A new caller-owned array, 32 bytes for V1 or 64 bytes for V2. Clear it after the last operation that uses it.</description></item>
            </list>
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentNullException">If <paramref name="peerCoseKey"/> is null.</exception>
            <remarks>
            The V1/V2 helper explicitly checks coordinate types and lengths, but currently does not
            validate the required kty, alg and crv labels or the optional-parameter restriction.
            Curve-point validation is delegated to the cryptographic provider; this limitation does
            not relax CTAP's required key structure. Each call generates a fresh ephemeral key pair.
            </remarks>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If a coordinate is missing, has the wrong type or length, or ECDH derivation raises a cryptographic error.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.Security.Cryptography.CryptographicException">A cryptographic provider may reject the peer key during import, before the derivation error is wrapped.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol.Kdf(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Derives a symmetric key from a raw ECDH shared secret using the protocol's KDF.
            </summary>
            <param name="z">The borrowed raw ECDH secret: the 32-byte big-endian X coordinate of the shared point. V1/V2 currently reject only empty input, not other lengths.</param>
            <returns>A new caller-owned array: SHA-256(z), 32 bytes, for V1; HMAC key || AES key, 64 bytes, for V2. Clear both the input secret and this result when no longer needed.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If <paramref name="z"/> is empty.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol.Encrypt(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Encrypts plaintext using AES-256-CBC without padding.
            </summary>
            <param name="key">The borrowed, already-derived shared secret: 32 bytes for V1 or 64 bytes for V2, which uses the final 32 bytes as its AES key. This method does not call Kdf.</param>
            <param name="plaintext">The borrowed plaintext, a nonempty multiple of 16 bytes. PIN right-zero-padding to 64 bytes is performed by ClientPin, not by AES.</param>
            <returns>A new caller-owned array: N bytes of ciphertext for V1, or a 16-byte random IV || N bytes of ciphertext for V2, where N is the plaintext length.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If the key length is invalid or plaintext is not a nonempty multiple of 16 bytes.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol.Decrypt(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Decrypts ciphertext using AES-256-CBC without removing padding or verifying integrity.
            </summary>
            <param name="key">The borrowed, already-derived shared secret: 32 bytes for V1 or 64 bytes for V2, which uses the final 32 bytes as its AES key. This method does not call Kdf.</param>
            <param name="ciphertext">Borrowed V1 ciphertext, a nonempty multiple of 16 bytes; or V2 IV || ciphertext, at least 32 bytes and a multiple of 16 bytes.</param>
            <returns>A new caller-owned plaintext array: the input length for V1, or the input length minus 16 for V2. Clear it when no longer needed.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If the key or ciphertext length is invalid.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol.Authenticate(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Computes an authentication tag (MAC) over a message.
            </summary>
            <param name="key">A borrowed token or derived shared secret: 16 or 32 bytes for V1; 32 or 64 bytes for V2, which uses the first 32 bytes as its HMAC key.</param>
            <param name="message">The borrowed message to authenticate; it may be empty.</param>
            <returns>
            A new caller-owned, secret-derived tag: the first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA-256 for V1,
            or all 32 bytes for V2. Clear it after its last use.
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If the key length is invalid.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.IPinUvAuthProtocol.Verify(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>
            Checks a local authentication tag using a constant-time comparison for equal-length tags.
            </summary>
            <param name="key">The borrowed token or shared secret accepted by Authenticate.</param>
            <param name="message">The borrowed message that was authenticated.</param>
            <param name="signature">The borrowed tag: 16 bytes for V1 or 32 bytes for V2.</param>
            <returns>True if the tag matches; false for a mismatch or wrong tag length. This does not check device token validity, permissions, RP binding or expiry.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">If the tag has the expected length but the key length is invalid.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinRetryStatus">
            <summary>
            Represents the authenticator's current PIN retry status.
            </summary>
            <remarks>A snapshot, not permission to retry. PIN_AUTH_BLOCKED requires a power cycle; PIN_BLOCKED means retries are exhausted and reset is required.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinRetryStatus.RetriesRemaining">
            <summary>
            Gets the parsed PIN retry count, currently defaulted to zero if the response omits it.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinRetryStatus.PowerCycleRequired">
            <summary>
            Gets the parsed power-cycle indication, currently defaulted to false if omitted.
            </summary>
            <remarks>CTAP defines omission as unknown. False does not prove a power cycle is unnecessary or a PIN attempt is safe; this model does not distinguish omission from explicit false.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthHelpers">
            <summary>
            Shared helpers for PIN/UV authentication protocol implementations.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Encapsulates the common ECDH P-256 key agreement logic used by both V1 and V2 protocols.
            The raw shared secret (Z) is returned to the caller, who applies protocol-specific KDF.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthHelpers.PerformEcdhKeyAgreement(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.Int32,System.Object})">
            <summary>
            Performs ECDH P-256 key agreement with the peer's COSE key.
            </summary>
            <param name="peerCoseKey">The borrowed peer key, required by CTAP to contain kty=2, alg=-25, crv=1 and 32-byte big-endian X/Y coordinates, without other optional parameters.</param>
            <returns>
            A new platform public-key dictionary and a caller-owned raw ECDH secret (Z), the 32-byte
            big-endian X coordinate of the shared point. Clear Z after deriving protocol-specific keys,
            including when that derivation fails. Public coordinates are not secret material.
            </returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentNullException">Thrown when <paramref name="peerCoseKey"/> is null.</exception>
            <remarks>
            Explicit checks currently cover only coordinate types and lengths, not required COSE labels
            or optional-parameter restrictions. Import forces P-256 and delegates point validation to the
            provider. The ephemeral crypto objects are disposed, but allocation of the public dictionary
            after derivation is not protected by a Z-clearing guard.
            </remarks>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">Thrown for missing/invalid coordinate types or lengths, or a wrapped cryptographic error from raw-secret derivation.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.Security.Cryptography.CryptographicException">Peer-key import can raise an unwrapped provider error before the derivation catch.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1">
            <summary>
            PIN/UV authentication protocol version 1 implementation.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            V1 uses:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>ECDH P-256 for key agreement</description></item>
              <item><description>SHA-256 of raw ECDH output as shared secret (32 bytes)</description></item>
              <item><description>AES-256-CBC with zero IV and no AES padding</description></item>
              <item><description>HMAC-SHA-256 for authentication (truncated to 16 bytes)</description></item>
            </list>
            </para>
            <para>
            V1 uses the same 32-byte shared secret for AES and HMAC. V2 derives separate keys, prefixes
            ciphertext with a random IV, and uses full 32-byte tags. Callers may prefer V2 when both sides
            support it; constructing this object does not negotiate a protocol with the authenticator.
            </para>
            <para>
            The instance retains no keys. Dispose marks it disposed: cryptographic operations then throw,
            while Version and AuthenticationTagLength remain readable. Caller-owned outputs are not cleared
            by disposal. Encapsulate clears its raw ECDH secret after derivation, and AES operations clear
            their temporary key/input arrays; this is not an end-to-end or all-exception-path cleanup guarantee.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#pinProto1
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1.Version">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1.AuthenticationTagLength">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1.Encapsulate(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.Int32,System.Object})">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1.Kdf(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1.Encrypt(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1.Decrypt(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1.Authenticate(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1.Verify(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV1.Dispose">
            <summary>Marks this instance disposed without clearing caller-owned inputs or outputs.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV2">
            <summary>
            PIN/UV authentication protocol version 2 implementation.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            V2 uses:
            <list type="bullet">
              <item><description>ECDH P-256 for key agreement</description></item>
              <item><description>Two independent HKDF-SHA-256 derivations with info "CTAP2 HMAC key" and "CTAP2 AES key", each producing 32 bytes (64 bytes total)</description></item>
              <item><description>AES-256-CBC with random IV and no AES padding</description></item>
              <item><description>HMAC-SHA-256 for authentication (full 32-byte output)</description></item>
            </list>
            </para>
            <para>
            The shared secret structure for V2:
            <code>
            sharedSecret[0..31]  = HMAC key (32 bytes)
            sharedSecret[32..63] = AES key (32 bytes)
            </code>
            </para>
            <para>
            CTAP 2.1 specifies a 32-zero-byte HKDF salt. The empty salt used here is HMAC-equivalent;
            the two derivations are not a single 64-byte HKDF expansion. Select this protocol only when
            the authenticator advertises support for version 2.
            </para>
            <para>
            The instance retains no keys. Dispose marks it disposed: cryptographic operations then throw,
            while Version and AuthenticationTagLength remain readable. Caller-owned outputs are not cleared
            by disposal. Encapsulate clears its raw ECDH secret and Kdf clears partially derived output on
            failure; AES clears its named temporary arrays, not every possible failed output or provider copy.
            </para>
            <para>
            See: https://fidoalliance.org/specs/fido-v2.1-ps-20210615/fido-client-to-authenticator-protocol-v2.1-ps-errata-20220621.html#pinProto2
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV2.Version">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV2.AuthenticationTagLength">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV2.Encapsulate(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.Int32,System.Object})">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV2.Kdf(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.Pin.PinUvAuthProtocolV2.Encrypt(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
